 15.
Notices of Motion
 15.1
Notice of Motion re: Federation of Canadian Municipalities (FCM) Board of Directors 
 Moved by: Mayor Brown

Seconded by: Deputy Mayor Singh

Whereas the Federation of Canadian Municipalities (FCM) represents the interests of of over 2,000 member municipalities across Canada, on policy and program matters that fall within federal jurisdiction;

Whereas FCM’s Board of Directors is comprised of elected municipal officials from all regions and sizes of communities to form a broad base of support and provide FCM with the united voice required to carry the municipal message to the federal government;

Whereas Councillor Rowena Santos represents the City of Brampton, Canada’s seventh-largest city, at the national advocacy table of FCM, advocating for municipal priorities and policies of importance to Brampton residents, including federal housing infrastructure investments and bail reform legislation such as Bill C-14;

Whereas FCM’s Annual Conference and Trade Show will be held Thursday, June 10 - Sunday, June 13, 2027, during which time the Annual General Meeting will be held, followed by the election of FCM’s Board of Directors; and

Whereas Councillor Rowena Santos has been elected and has served on the FCM Board for the past 6 years, recognized as an FCM municipal trailblazer, and currently serves as Chair of the Community Safety and Crime Prevention committee and has served as Chair of the Municipal Finance, Infrastructure and Transportation Committee, Vice-Chair of the Municipal Finance and Intergovernmental Relations Committee, Vice-Chair of the Anti-Racism and Equity Committee for 2 terms, is a member of the Infrastructure and Transportation Committee among others; and has consistently championed motions at FCM, advocated for Brampton priorities, and presented best practice examples of Brampton’s work at every Board Meeting; 

Be It Resolved that Council of the City of Brampton endorse Councillor Rowena Santos, to continue serving on FCM’s Board of Directors for the remainder of the board term ending in June 2027, and support her re-election to FCM’s Board of Directors at the 2027 and 2029 FCM Annual General Meetings.
