Virtual Council & Planning Meetings
Council and Planning meetings are held in a hybrid format, with options to attend in person or online. Meetings are livestreamed and recorded for public viewing through this Council Portal and on the Municipality's YouTube channel.

If you are participating virtually and wish to speak during Citizen Comments or the Question Period, please register with the Clerk's Department in advance of the meeting. Participation details will be provided upon registration. For assistance, contact clerks@brighton.ca.

Meeting Recordings & Privacy
Meeting recordings are available for public viewing through this portal. Please be aware that comments made during a meeting may be recorded and form part of the public record. While the Municipality strives to provide reliable livestreaming, technical issues may occasionally affect service. Livestreaming is provided as a convenience to support public access and transparency; however, technical difficulties do not affect the conduct or validity of a meeting.

