 11.1
Municipal Election
 Electors can vote in the Municipal and School Board Election by internet or telephone from Monday, October 19, 2026 at 10:00 a.m. until Monday, October 26, 2026 at 8:00 p.m. The Official List of Certified Candidates is available on the Municipality's website.

Residents can contact the Voter Help Centre by email, phone 519-881-2223, or visit the Municipal Office prior to the Election to confirm if they are on the Voters List and/or have their information updated.

A Voter Help Centre will also be available during the voting period for electors requiring assistance to vote, or for individuals that would like to add or update their information on the Voters List. Learn more at Brockton.ca/Election.
11.2
Little Royal Fair
 The Walkerton Agricultural Society is hosting the Annual Little Royal Fair on October 16-18, 2026 at the Agricultural Buildings in Walkerton (206 Durham St.). This year's theme is Home for the Harvest, and a weekend full of entertainment is planned for the whole family! Visit the Walkerton Agricultural Society's website or social media accounts for more information!
11.3
Elmwood Halloween Trail
 The Elmwood Community Service Association invite you to their Halloween Trail on Sunday, October 25, 2026 from 10:00 a.m. to Noon at the Elmwood Community Centre basement hall!
11.4
Walkerton & District Optimist Club Monster March Parade
 The Walkerton & District Optimist Club invite you to their Monster March Parade on Sunday, October 25, 2026 at 2:00 p.m. The parade starts at Riverbend Park along Jackson and Durham Streets ending at the Market Garden park! 

Road Closure: Jackson St. N. will be closed from Durham St. E to the corner of Durham & Victoria St. between 1:30 and 4:30 p.m. for the parade.
11.5
Hometown Christmas Market
 The Hometown Christmas Market returns on Thursday, November 19, 2026 from 4:00 to 9:00 p.m., bringing festive cheer to every corner of Durham Street. Local businesses will be open late, and you’ll find more than 30 vendors offering unique gifts, tasty treats, and holiday treasures. Gather in the Market Garden at 5:30 p.m. for the tree lighting ceremony, then stay to enjoy live music, delicious food trucks, and a cozy licensed area hosted by the Walkerton District Hospital Foundation. Don’t miss your chance to win big in the Hometown Holiday Hunt, with dozens of prizes waiting to be discovered! 

Road Closure: Durham Street between Jackson and Victoria Streets in Walkerton will be closed to traffic starting at 2:00 p.m. on November 19th to accommodate shoppers and festivities. The road will reopen by 10:00 p.m.
11.6
Santa Claus Parade
 The Walkerton Kinsmen Club will be hosting the annual Walkerton Santa Claus Parade on Saturday, November 28, 2026 at 7:00 p.m. along Durham St., Walkerton.

Road Closure: Durham St. will be closed from Victoria St. to the Walkerton Community Centre (201 Durham St. W.) from 6:45 to 9:00 p.m. for the parade.
11.7
Elmwood Christmas in the Park
 Join the Elmwood Community Service Association on Sunday, November 29, 2026 at 3:30 p.m. at the Lions' Park for pictures with Santa and Mrs. Claus, and crafts, popcorn, hot chocolate and coffee in the park. The Christmas Tree will be lit up at 5:00 p.m.
11.8
Tax Due Date
 The final 2026 Brockton Tax Installment is due on November 30, 2026.
