 11.1
The Secret Path Screening and Walk for Wenjack
This item has Video
 The Bruce County Public Library Walkerton Branch is showing a screening of The Secret Path at 6:00 p.m. on Tuesday, September 29, 2026. The Secret Path is a poignant animated film based on the album by Gord Downie and the graphic novel by Jeff Lemire about Chanie Wenjack’s story and the legacy of residential schools in Canada.

The Municipality of Brockton is hosting a joint National Day for Truth and Reconciliation Vigil/Walk for Wenjack on Wednesday, September 30, 2026 at 6:00 p.m. at Riverbend Park, Walkerton. Light refreshments will be provided. Donations to the Nawash Food Bank and Saugeen First Nations will be accepted onsite.
11.2
Municipal Offices Closed for Thanksgiving
This item has Video
 Municipal Offices will be closed on Monday, October 12, 2026 for Thanksgiving. Our offices will reopen on Tuesday, October 13, 2026. Council and staff wish you a safe and happy holiday weekend!
11.3
Municipal Election
This item has Video
 Electors can vote in the Municipal and School Board Election by internet or telephone from Monday, October 19, 2026 at 10:00 a.m. until Monday, October 26, 2026 at 8:00 p.m. The Official List of Certified Candidates is available on the Municipality's website.

Residents can contact the Voter Help Centre by email, phone 519-881-2223, or visit the Municipal Office prior to the Election to confirm if they are on the Voters List and/or have their information updated.

A Voter Help Centre will also be available during the voting period for electors requiring assistance to vote, or for individuals that would like to add or update their information on the Voters List. Learn more at Brockton.ca/Election.
