Simcoe County Warden Basil Clarke re: Leachate Disposal
  Staff recommendation:
WHEREAS The Town of Collingwood agreement to accept hauled leachate from the County of Simcoe landfill locations has lapsed and a new, time limited Extra Strength Surcharge Agreement (ESSA) needs to be established;
AND WHEREAS the Town of Collingwood has concerns the County of Simcoe has secured limited locations and access where they have contracted permission to dispose of the landfill leachate;
AND WHEREAS the Town of Collingwood is refining the financial cost of receiving and treating hauled wastewater at the wastewater treatment plant and recognizes current work to commence study and design for a wastewater treatment plant expansion will likely result in revised effluent criteria, additional processes, and related capital and operating costs associated with meeting higher effluent criteria;
BE IT RESOLVED the Town of Collingwood advises the County of Simcoe they are notified that a revised and updated ESSA must be signed by December 9, 2026;
AND THAT the Town of Collingwood will not accept leachate from the ORO Landfill on weekdays and will only accept ORO leachate on weekends and during emergency situations, subject to quantity and quality provisions set out in the new ESSA, and be approved in advance by Town Staff (Supervisor, Wastewater) as of December 9, 2026;
AND THAT the new ESSA will include required additional testing of leachate, at the cost of the County of Simcoe, and provisions for the County of Simcoe to be an active participant in the wastewater treatment plant expansion project through study, design and construction for processes related to contaminant testing, treatment and removal;
AND THAT the Town of Collingwood will continue to accept leachate from all other County of Simcoe landfills, subject to quantity, quality and receiving provisions set out in the new ESSA, including conditions around emergency situations requiring Town Staff approval in advance (Supervisor, Wastewater) until June 30, 2027, with the ability to terminate within 30 days notice (both parties) and the ability to renew the agreement prior to the end date.
