WELCOME
Welcome to our Meeting and Information Portal! We pride ourselves on being accessible to all our citizens, and providing information to people as easily as possible. Through our Portal you will be able to subscribe to meeting updates, search documents and find out when our next meeting is scheduled. See below for more information about what you can do in our Portal.

Review the Meeting Calendar
By visiting the Calendar you can review the dates and times of different meetings that are scheduled. If the agenda has been published, the calendar will include a link to the meeting documents.

View Meeting Details
Visit the Meetings page to view the types of meetings held at the Township of Greater Madawaska. Each meeting type will also include links to recently published meeting documents.

Search our Online Library
Our CivicWeb Portal has a built in search function that allows you to enter keywords and search for documents related to your keywords. This is especially useful when looking for a specific document or information on a specific topic, such as a bylaw.

Subscribe to Meeting Updates
Also included in the Portal is the ability to sign up for automatic email notifications. When an agenda or minutes package is published you can receive an email notice that contains a link to the published documents.
 View Live Streamed Meetings
Council meetings are Live Streamed on the Township's YouTube Channel.  You can watch meetings live or view previously recorded meetings. 
 View By-Laws
Visit the Township Website to view frequently requested By-laws or to request a copy of other By-laws.
By-laws are also continuously being added to the Portal Document Centre for public viewing.
 Meet Council Members
Visit the Township's Website to meet our Council Members.
 Speak to Council
The Township of Greater Madawaska welcomes your voice and opinion. You may request to be a delegation to speak before Council, by submitting an application form.  Check the Meeting Calendar for upcoming Council meeting dates, then read, complete and submit the Delegation Information and Request Form. Your request must be received by 8:30am on the Thursday of the week prior to the meeting date.
  Need help using one of the tools on our Portal?
Visit our Help section by clicking on Help in the top right corner, then select CivicWeb Help from the drop down.

