2026-203

A By-law of the City of Greater Sudbury to Set an Interim Tax Levy and Tax Billing Dates Prior to the Development of the 2027 Tax Policy

City Council Resolution #CC2026-98

Section 317(1) of the Municipal Act, 2001, provides the authority for an interim tax levy prior to the adoption of the final estimates. In addition to approving the interim tax levy, interim due dates have been established as February 26, 2027 and March 31, 2027.
14.
Members' Motions
  14.1
Committee Structure
  As presented by Mayor Lefebvre:

WHEREAS the City of Greater Sudbury has a number of standing Committees that receive reports and presentations from various City departments;

AND WHEREAS it can be challenging for members that are not appointed to certain committees to attend and participate in the discussion of important matters on committee agendas;

AND WHEREAS combining certain Committees into a single Committee comprised of the whole of Council would increase efficiency, reduce duplication of debate and make it easier for all members to participate;

NOW THEREFORE BE IT RESOLVED that staff be directed to present the required bylaw amendments to combine the Finance and Administration Committee, Community and Emergency Services Committee, Operations Committee and  Nominations Committee into a new Committee comprised of all members of Council entitled Committee of the Whole which Committee shall meet regularly on the third Tuesday of each month at 4 or 6 p.m. at the discretion of the Clerk;

AND BE IT FURTHER RESOLVED that the mandate of the Committee of the Whole include the mandate of the Committees being replaced and be the primary forum for policy debate on issues within the City’s area of jurisdiction, with the exception of those matters specifically within the mandate of other Committees;

AND BE IT FURTHER RESOLVED that the open meetings of the Committee of the Whole be chaired by the Mayor and that any closed meetings be Chaired by the Deputy Mayors in accordance with the Procedure By-Law;  

AND BE IT FURTHER RESOLVED that the bylaw amendments to be presented include the reallocation of annual remuneration for the Chairs of the Finance and Administration Committee, Community and Emergency Services Committee, Operations Committee and Nominations Committee to the members of the Planning Committee with the revised remuneration as follows:

Planning Committee Chair - $9,000.00

Planning Committee Vice-Chair - $4,500.00

Planning Committee Member - $3,500.00

AND BE IT FURTHER RESOLVED that the bylaw amendments to be presented discontinue the Hearing Committee and that the mandate of the Hearing Committee be combined into the terms of reference for the Planning Committee.
