 7.1
Recreation Services
 a.
Overnight Camping Request in Rotary Park
 The Municipality of Kincardine has By-law No. 2002 – 145, which prohibits overnight camping in public places and Municipal parks owned by The Corporation of the Municipality of Kincardine. The Municipality received a request from Rotary District 6330 for an exemption to this by-law which would allow their Interact and Youth Exchange Students to camp overnight at Rotary Park from June 13-15, 2019 in conjunction with the Rotary District 6330 Conference taking place in Kincardine at that time. Along with camping overnight, they would require access to washrooms/showers, as well as hydro and water. Staff is recommending that Council authorize the exemption for the period requested above.
b.
Recreational Advertising & Financial Assistance Programs
 A proposal is being presented to implement recreational advertising to generate additional revenue for the Municipality which could then be used to support families and individuals with access to recreation and leisure programs through the creation of a financial assistance program. Staff are seeking support to develop and Advertising Policy and a Recreation and Culture Financial Assistance Program.
7.2
Other Areas of Responsibility
 a.
Bruce Road 20 and Farrell Drive Street Lighting Request
 7ACRES and Bruce Power have approached the County and the Municipality to address safety concerns at the intersection of Bruce Road 20 and Farrell Drive.
Delegation: Dan Piggott - 7 Acres 
b.
Structure 2206 (Broadway St. Bridge) Tender
 The repairs to structure 2206 on Broadway Street Bridge were included in the 2019 Capital Budget Plan. The scope of work includes repairs to the east end of the south girder and to the bearing seat at the west end of the south girder. One bid was received and was reviewed by our municipal engineer. 
c.
Bruce County Waste Management Update
 The Waste Management Update Report is for information. Due to legislative changes, a number of programs are being amended.
d.
Huronville Generator
 The purpose of this report is to update Council on the cost sharing agreement with the Township of Huron-Kinloss for the installation of a permanent back-up generator at the Huronville Well Site for the Huron-Kinloss Lakeshore Distribution System
