BY-LAW NO. 4138-2025 
 
BEING a by-law to establish and impose tax rates for the purpose of raising the general 
municipal, county and education levies for the year 2025; 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
WHEREAS the estimates of all sums that may be required for the lawful purpose of the 
Corporation of the Township of Montague for the year 2025 have been adopted by the 
Municipal Council by virtue of By-Law No. 4113-2025 and section 290 of the Municipal 
Act, 2001 S.O. 2001, c.25. as amended;  
 
AND WHEREAS the property assessment roll for the Township of Montague on which 
2025 taxes are to be levied has been provided pursuant to the Assessment Act, R.S.O. 
1990, c. A.31, as amended;  
 
AND WHEREAS pursuant to the County of Lanark By-law 2025-10, the County of Lanark 
passed a by-law to set tax ratios and to set tax rate reductions for prescribed property 
classes for upper tier purposes and local municipal purposes for the year 2025; 
 
AND WHEREAS pursuant to the County of Lanark By-law 2025-11, the County of Lanark 
passed a by-law to establish 2025 tax rates to be levied to local municipalities; 
 
AND WHEREAS the Province of Ontario has regulated all education tax rates for 2025; 
 
AND WHEREAS section 311 and 312 of the Municipal Act, dictates that for the purposes 
of raising the general local municipal levy and the county levy, the council of a local 
municipality shall, each year, pass a by-law levying a separate tax rate, as specified in 
the by-law, on the assessment in each property class in the local municipality rateable for 
local and upper tier purposes; 
 
NOW THEREFORE, the Council of the Corporation of the Township of Montague enacts 
as follows: 
 
1. 
THAT the tax rates for the year 2025, as shown on the Schedule “A” attached, are 
hereby assessed, levied and imposed on the whole rateable property assessments 
within the Township of Montague and the levying and collecting of said rates are 
hereby authorized and directed. 
 
2. 
THAT the Interim Tax Levy pursuant to By-law Number 4106-2024 shall be shown 
as a reduction on the final tax levy. 
 
3. 
THAT the First Response fire rate for the area of the Township of Montague, as set 
out in By-law No. 3715-2019, and served by the Village of Merrickville-Wolford Fire 
Department shall be as follows: 
- 
Residential/Farm unit - $23.00 

- 
Residential/Farm Vacant unit - $11.50 
 
4. 
THAT the net amount of the taxes levied by this by-law shall be due and payable in 
two installments.  The first installment shall be due and payable on the last business 
day of August 2025 and the second installment shall be due and payable on the last 
business day of October 2025. 
 
5. 
THAT the above dates shall in no way preclude the requirement to pay the interim 
tax levy on the last business day of March 2025 and the last business day of June 
2025 for all taxpayers. 
 
6. 
THAT payment of taxes may be made at all chartered financial institutions, via the 
Internet, telephone banking or over the counter. 
 
7. 
THAT if taxes are not paid on the due dates, a penalty of one and one-quarter 
percent (1.25%) of the unpaid taxes shall be levied on the first day of the calendar 
month following the due date and a further penalty of one and one-quarter percent 
(1.25%) on the first day of each month thereafter for so long as the default continues, 
but not after December 31st, 2025. 
 
8. 
THAT if any taxes levied pursuant to this by-law remain unpaid as of January 1st, 
2026, interest at the rate of one and one-quarter percent (1.25%) of the unpaid taxes 
shall be charged on January 1st, 2026 and also on the first day of each calendar 
month thereafter for as long as the default continues. 
 
9. 
THAT By-law 4135-2025 be repealed in its entirety. 
 
10. THAT where any by-law, passed prior to this by-law, conflicts with the terms of this 
by-law, this by-law shall prevail. 
 
11. THAT this by-law comes into force and takes effect on the date of its passing. 
 
 
READ A FIRST, SECOND & THIRD TIME & PASSED, SIGNED & SEALED THIS 15TH 
