• Of the total additional jobs identified for the County of Oxford over the long term 
to 2061, approximately 78% of jobs are anticipated to have a usual place of work, 
while the remaining 22% of new jobs are associated with work at home 
employment or off-site employees. 
• With respect to employment by major sector, approximately 61% of job growth 
for the County is associated with services-producing sectors, while 39% of jobs 
are associated with goods-producing sectors (i.e., industrial and primary 
employment sectors). 
