 4.4.1
Report to Council - Request for Community Centre Fee Relief - MAMAS Halloween Event
 Prepared by: Denis Turcot, CAO
Recommended Resolution
BE IT RESOLVED THAT Council for the Municipality of St.-Charles approves a one-time waiver of the Community Centre rental fee for the Moms Adding Magic Across St.-Charles (MAMAS) to host the Boo Bash & Monster Mash – St.-Charles Family Halloween event, subject to the following conditions:
The Community Centre must be left in a clean and orderly condition following the event.
The event must be open and free of charge to the general public.
The primary purpose of the event must be to provide a family and youth-oriented community activity of general public interest.
No fundraising activities may take place during the event without Council approval.
The organizer must comply with all other applicable municipal rental requirements, including proof of insurance and payment of any required damage deposit.
AND BE IT FURTHER RESOLVED THAT Moms Adding Magic Across St.-Charles (MAMAS) be added to the Municipality’s list of eligible organizations qualifying for a 10% discount on future facility rentals, subject to the Municipality’s applicable rental policies and conditions.
