  AGENDA

THE INAUGURAL MEETING OF THE ONE HUNDRED AND FORTY-SEVENTH COUNCIL OF THE CORPORATION OF THE CITY OF ST. THOMAS
November 16, 2026 at 5:00 P.M.
COUNCIL CHAMBERS/ZOOM
ROUTINE PROCEEDINGS AND GENERAL ORDERS OF THE DAY

CALL TO ORDER
LAND ACKNOWLEDGEMENT STATEMENT       
DECLARATION OF ELECTION
DECLARATIONS OF ELECTED OFFICE AND OATH OF ALLEGIANCE
MAYOR'S INAUGURAL ADDRESS
APPOINTMENT OF BANK SIGNING OFFICERS
ADJOURNMENT
1.
CALL TO ORDER
 The members will assemble in Committee Room 304.  The City Clerk will announce the Call to Order.

Council will enter the Chambers led by His Worship Jeff Kohler accompanied by Piper Rob Angus. 
2.
LAND ACKNOWLEDGEMENT
 We acknowledge that the land on which we meet is the traditional territory of the Haudenosaunee, Anishinabek, Attiwonderonk (Neutral) and Mississauga peoples and is now home to many diverse First Nations, Inuit and Métis peoples.

We also recognize that this land is now home to the Munsee-Delaware Nation, Chippewas of the Thames First Nation and Oneida Nation of the Thames.

This land was settled through Treaty 2, the McKee Purchase Treaty of 1790, and we, as beneficiaries of the treaty recognize our collective responsibilities to the land and water.
3.
DECLARATION OF OFFICE
 The City Clerk will declare the result of the vote of the regular election held on October 26th, 2026.
4.
DECLARATIONS OF ELECTED OFFICE AND OATH OF ALLEGIANCE
 His Worship Mayor Jeff Kohler will publicly subscribe his declaration of office and oath of allegiance and receive the Chain of Office.

The members of Council, in unison, will publicly subscribe their declaration of office of oath of allegiance.
5.
MAYOR'S INAUGURAL ADDRESS
 His Worship Jeff Kohler will thereupon deliver his address.

A motion for consideration of the address of His Worship the Mayor will be presented.
6.
APPOINTMENT OF SIGNING OFFICERS
 A motion of appointment of the Corporation's signing officers will be presented.
7.
ADJOURNMENT
