 9.
Notices of Motion
This item has Video
 9.1
Councillor Steve Pelkman
This item has Video
 Where as the Province of Ontario has changed the Provincial Planning Statement to encourage intensification and that the Municipality of Strathroy-Caradoc has been receiving applications that we may consider over-intensification for the character of the neighbourhood with minimal setbacks. And that these proposals may be circumventing other proposals by developers who have invested in properties that are appropriate for the size of the building being proposed.
Recommendation
THAT: Strathroy-Caradoc staff prepare a report that outlines potential solutions and the process to implement changes to the Zoning By-law that would require side and rear yard setbacks to scale based on the height of the proposal, and further;

THAT: the wording of those provisions be applied to the height of the building in meters above grade, and further;

THAT: the report and recommendation come back to Council by the December 7, 2026 Council meeting.
9.2
Councillor Greg Willsie
This item has Video
 WHEREAS construction and alterations are currently taking place at the Caradoc Community Centre, including the apparent conversion of the existing coat/boot room into office space;

AND WHEREAS the Caradoc Community Centre is a municipal community facility that serves residents, community organizations, and facility users;

AND WHEREAS Council should be informed of significant changes to the use or configuration of municipal facilities, including the purpose, cost, funding source, operational impacts, and any impacts on existing services or amenities;

THEREFORE BE IT RESOLVED
Recommendation
THAT: Council direct staff to provide a report to Council regarding the construction and alterations currently taking place at the Caradoc Community Centre, including:
A description of all work currently underway or planned at the facility, including the purpose and rationale for each alteration;
The total estimated cost of the work, including construction, materials, internal labour, furnishings, equipment, professional services, and any other associated costs;
The approved budget and funding source for the work, including identification of any operating or capital budget accounts being used;
The authority under which the work was initiated, including any Council resolution, approved capital project, delegated authority, procurement authority, or other authorization relied upon;
An explanation of the intended use of the office space being created, including which staff or municipal function will occupy the space and why office space at the Caradoc Community Centre is required;
An explanation of how the existing function of the coat/boot room will be accommodated following its conversion to office space, particularly during large community events and rentals;
Details of any consultation undertaken with facility users, community organizations, or the public prior to making the changes, and if no consultation occurred, an explanation of why it was not considered necessary; and
Any anticipated impact the alterations may have on the capacity, functionality, rental use, or future programming of the Caradoc Community Centre, and further;
THAT: the report identify any additional alterations currently contemplated for the Caradoc Community Centre that have not yet been presented to Council.
