Recreation Services 
Page | 1 
 
Recreation Services 
005-2023-RS 
Memo 
To: 
Mayor and Council 
From: 
Mathew Bahm, Director of Recreation 
Date: 
March 21, 2023 
Subject: 
NISKA Park Frogs Breath Application 
Attachments: 
Letter from the NISKA Leadership Centre 
 
Mayor and Council: 
 
The City has received a request from the NISKA Leadership Centre to sponsor a 
request for funding to the Frog’s Breath Foundation.  Their funding request would be to 
help with costs associated with development of Niska Park on the Haileybury 
Waterfront.  The City is already a partner on this project with the NIKSA Leadership 
Centre. 
 
If successful, NISKA would receive $25,000 to put towards outdoor park equipment. 
 
The Frog’s Breath Foundation requires that applicants who are not a registered charity 
partner with a community agency who can accept charitable donations and provide tax 
receipts. 
 
The City has sponsored applications to the Frogs Breath Foundation multiple times in 
the past and have had no issues with organizations fulfilling their reporting requirements 
under the City’s Charitable Sponsorship Policy, By-law 2018-039. 
 
It is recommended that the City agree to sponsor this application to the Frog’s Breath 
Foundation in support of the NISKA Leadership Centre. 
 
 
 
 
Prepared by: 
 
 
“Original signed by” 
 
Mathew Bahm 
Director of Recreation 
 
Reviewed and submitted for Council’s 
consideration by: 
 
“Original signed by” 
 
Amy Vickery 
City Manager 
 
 

 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
Mayor and Council 
City of Temiskaming Shores 
325 Farr Drive 
Haileybury, ON POJ IKO 
 
Wednesday March 15, 2023 
 
Le Centre de Leadership NISKA Leadership Centre (NISKA) is applying to the Frog’s Breath 
Foundation’s March 31, 2023 deadline for funding in the amount of $25,000 to purchase playground 
equipment, outdoor musical instruments, and accessible outdoor fitness equipment for Parc NISKA 
Park. 
 
Although we are incorporated as a not-for-profit organisation, NISKA is not a registered charitable 
organization.  As such, the Frog’s Breath Foundation requests that we obtain sponsorship from an 
organisation or Municipality to receive funds. 
 
Therefore, on behalf of NISKA, it is respectfully requested that the City of Temiskaming Shores act as 
sponsor for our application to the Frog’s Breath Foundation. 
 
Sincerely, 
 
 
 
Felicity Buckell 
For NISKA 
Le Centre de Leadership 
NISKA Leadership Centre 
PO Box 1380 
Haileybury, ON P0J 1K0 
705-650-2099 

 
Corporate Services 
Page | 1 
 
Corporate Services 
010-2023-CS 
Memo 
To: 
Mayor and Council 
From: 
James Franks 
Date: 
March 21, 2023 
Subject: 
Frog’s Breath Application Sponsorship – One Light in 
Temiskaming 
Attachments: 
Email from One Light in Temiskaming  
 
Mayor and Council: 
 
The City has received a request from the One Light in Temiskaming to sponsor a request 
for funding support to the Frog’s Breath Foundation, to help fund monthly multicultural 
events, cross-cultural learning courses and English conversation circles.  If successful, 
the One Light in Temiskaming would receive $10,000 to put towards this project. The 
Frog’s Breath Foundation and other community funding organizations often require that 
applicants who are not a registered charity partner with a community agency who can 
accept charitable donations and provide tax receipts. 
 
The City has sponsored applications for other community organizations in the past under 
the City’s Charitable Sponsorship Policy, Bylaw 2018-039.  This organization is new to 
our community so has not been supported in the past. 
 
It is recommended that the City agree to sponsor this application to the Frog’s Breath 
Foundation in support of the One Light in Temiskaming. 
 
 
Prepared by: 
 
 
“Original signed by” 
 
James Franks 
Economic Development 
Officer 
 
 
Reviewed and submitted for 
Council’s consideration by: 
 
“Original signed by” 
 
Amy Vickery Menard 
