7.4
REP-ENV-02-2026 Environmental Services Cost Allocation Policy
 Recommended resolution: 

Be it resolved that Council approve the Environmental Services Cost Allocation Policy attached as Attachment 1; and that Administration applies the policy in future budget and fee recommendations, review Environmental Charges By-law No. 108-2025 for alignment, and bring any required by-law or rate changes to Council before implementation.
7.5
Permit Building Statistics Reports for the months of September and October 2026
 Motion to receive the Permit Building Statistics Report for the months of September and October 2026.
7.6
REP-FIN-20-2026 - Properties to Vest
 Recommended resolution: 

Be it resolved that Council authorize the Treasurer to write off the outstanding taxes on the properties identified in this report and proceed with vesting the properties in the name of The Nation Municipality;

And that Administration be directed to explore opportunities to transfer the properties to interested regional or governmental partners, including the United Counties of Prescott and Russell (UCPR), South Nation Conservation Authority (SNC), or other public agencies;

And that any proposed transfer be completed at no cost to The Nation Municipality, with all associated legal, administrative and transfer costs borne by the receiving organization, in accordance with applicable legislation and municipal policies.

 7.7
REP-FIN-21-2026 - Property transfer to The Nation
 Proposed resolution: 

Be it resolved that Council authorize the Treasurer to write off the outstanding taxes on the property identified in this report and proceed with the property transfer in the name of The Nation Municipality;

And that any legal fees associated with the proposed transfer be absorbed by The Nation Municipality;

And that Administration be directed to explore opportunities to transfer the properties to interested regional or governmental partners, including the United Counties of Prescott and Russell (UCPR), South Nation Conservation Authority (SNC), or other public agencies.
