 5.2
Official Plan Amendment, Zoning By-law Amendment and Consent for Private Easements - Arundel Street
This item has Video
 
Confidential Memorandum dated August 4, 2026 from Joel DePeuter, Director Development Services relative to the above noted. (Distributed separately to City Council, City Manager, Commissioner – Growth, Commissioner – Corporate Services & City Treasurer and City Solicitor only). 

Report 324-2026 Growth-Development Services-Planning Services providing a recommendation relative to a Site-Specific Official Plan and Zoning By-law Amendment and Consent to create private easements on lands municipally known as 791 Arundel Street, for Council's consideration.

Written deputation received July 22, 2026 from Michelle Laponte and Daniel Lee relative to the above noted, for information.
WITH RESPECT to Report 324-2026-Growth-Development Services-Planning Services, we recommend that the Official Plan and Zoning By-law be amended on the subject lands, being Part of Lot C, Plan 59 McIntyre S. of Arundel St & E of 55R-3630 Except Plan 818, shown as “Property Location” on Attachment A to Report 324-2026, and municipally known as 791 Arundel Street;
AND THAT the subject lands be redesignated in the Official Plan from the Community Designation to the Residential Designation;
AND THAT the Zoning By-law be amended as it applies to the subject lands as follows:
i)      Rezone from the ""CM"" – Community Zone to the ""UM"" – Urban Mid-rise Zone with Site Specific Provision 116
ii)     Redefine a Lot to mean the lands contained by the boundaries shown and labeled UMSP116 
iii)    Delete the maximum front building setback on a Lot as re-defined;
AND THAT the authority delegated to the Committee of Adjustment be withdrawn with respect to consent to create private easements on the subject lands;
AND THAT consent for private easements for servicing and access across both proposed new parcels of land be approved conditionally for a period of two years ending on August 11, 2028, subject to the conditions in Attachment “D” to this report;
AND THAT the consent for private easements proceed to final approval to the satisfaction of the Secretary-Treasurer of the Committee of Adjustment;
AND THAT the lands be designated as an area of Site Plan Control;
AND THAT the Director - Development Services be authorized to execute any required Development Agreements;
AND THAT any necessary by-laws be presented to City Council for ratification.
