 9.
Petitions and Communications
This item has Video
 9.1
Northern Policing Costs
This item has Video
 
Memorandum dated July 24, 2026 from Chair, Inter-Governmental Affairs Committee Councillor Trevor Giertuga providing a Motion relative to the above noted. 
WITH RESPECT to the Memorandum from Councillor Trevor Giertuga, Chair – Inter-Governmental Affairs Committee, dated July 24, 2026, we recommend that the Government of Ontario commit to examining the cost pressures of policing for northern municipalities and undertake a comprehensive review and reform of the police funding model;
AND THAT the Province work collaboratively with northern municipalities to develop a sustainable, long-term framework to fund mandated policing services;
AND THAT a copy of this resolution be forwarded to the Premier of Ontario, the Minister of the Solicitor General, the Minister of Municipal Affairs and Housing, the Association of Municipalities of Ontario (AMO), and all Northern Ontario municipalities for their support;
AND THAT any necessary by-laws be presented to City Council for ratification.

9.2
Capital Funding Options - Infrastructure Deficit
This item has Video
 
Memorandum dated July 28, 2026 from Councillor Mark Bentz providing a Motion relative to the above noted.
WITH RESPECT to the Memorandum from Councillor Mark Bentz dated July 28, 2026, we recommend that Administration explore options that will increase the amount of funding being directed to capital renewal [KG1.1]with the goal of expediting the elimination of the City’s infrastructure funding gap;
AND THAT Administration develop a Municipal Price Index (MPI) framework specific to the City of Thunder Bay to be presented to City Council for consideration;
AND THAT recommendations to City Council be provided through an update to the Long-Range Financial Plan in Q1 2027;
AND THAT any necessary by-laws be presented to City Council for ratification.

9.3
Information on Sale of Parkland
This item has Video
 
Memorandum dated July 16, 2026 from Councillor Trevor Giertuga providing a Motion relative to the above noted.
WITH RESPECT to the Memorandum from Councillor Trevor Giertuga dated July 21, 2026, we recommend that City Council direct Administration to inform Council as early in the process as is practical about any parkland under consideration for surplus and sale prior to negotiations taking place between the City and a private or public entity; 
AND THAT Administration report back to Council on this subject each time a park be considered for surplus and sale;
AND THAT any necessary by-laws be sent to City Council for ratification.

9.4
Road Work - Mountain Road and 15th Side Road 
This item has Video
 
Memorandum dated July 20, 2026 from Councillor Greg Johnsen providing a Motion relative to the above noted.
WITH RESPECT to the Memorandum from Councillor Greg Johnsen dated July 20, 2026, we recommend that City Council direct Administration to prepare information on potential upgrades and costing for 15th Side Road from Mountain Road to Highway 61; 
AND THAT Administration also prepare information on potential upgrades and costing for Mountain Road from 15th Side Road to Highway 61;
AND THAT this information be presented to Council by the September 15, 2026 meeting;
AND THAT any necessary by-laws be sent to City Council for ratification.

9.5
Advocacy - Harmonization of Northern Road Construction Standards
This item has Video
 
Memorandum dated July 23, 2026 from Chair, Inter-Governmental Affairs Committee Councillor Trevor Giertuga providing a Motion relative to the above noted.
WITH RESPECT to the Memorandum from Councillor Trevor Giertuga, Chair – Inter-Governmental Affairs Committee, dated July 23, 2026, we recommend that a letter from the City Manager be sent to the Minister of Transportation with copies to relevant members of MTO staff and other municipal advocacy bodies, outlining the City of Thunder Bay's concerns relating to the proposed harmonization of the Ontario Provincial Standard Specifications for municipal road construction;
AND THAT the letter also express willingness to collaborate with the Province on a practical and flexible framework that reflects local conditions and specific needs of the municipality and ability to pursue appropriate innovative solutions; 
AND THAT any necessary by-laws be presented to City Council for ratification.

