THAT the pavilion option referred to in Resolution #2025-206 not proceed forward, until a complete pavilion proposal is brought forward for Council’s consideration, including an identified proponent, concept design and scope, detailed capital and operating budget, confirmed funding sources, required approvals, and a proposed ownership, construction, operation and maintenance agreement; and
THAT, further to consultation with Tillsonburg Minor Baseball Inc. where there is no longer a need for a scorer’s box and storage shed, Parks Capital Project #395 be amended to remove the Hardball 1 storage shed and the Hardball 1 scorer’s box; and
THAT staff be directed to allocate the removed $30,000 project funding in the Facilities Reserve for future ball diamond improvement projects.
13.6.3
Community Sport and Recreation Infrastructure Fund - Stream 1 - RCP-26-048
 THAT report RCP 26-048 titled “Community Sport and Recreation Infrastructure Fund – Stream 1” be received as information; and
THAT the Director of Recreation, Culture and Parks be directed to apply to the Community Sport and Recreation Infrastructure Fund - Stream 1: Repair and Rehabilitation grant program for the Memorial Arena Revitalization project, at a cost of up to $696,250; and
THAT the selected project be included in the 2028 capital budget for the Mayor’s consideration to meet the 50/50 cost sharing requirement.
13.6.4
ANHS Operational Hours Review- RCP-26-049
 THAT report RCP-26-049 titled “ANHS Operational Hours Review” be received as information; and
THAT an annual one-week public closure during the first business week of January be adopted as an operational practice at Annandale National Historic Site (ANHS); and
THAT Saturday public operating hours at ANHS between Victoria Day and August 31 be adopted as a permanent operational practice; and
THAT the extended Thursday operating hours between Victoria Day and August 31 be discontinued.
13.6.5
Parkland Protection Policy - RCP-26-053
 THAT report RCP 26-047 titled “Parkland Protection Policy” be received as information; and
THAT Council direct staff to prepare a Parkland Protection Policy, and to bring forward any related Official Plan, zoning, parkland dedication, land disposition or reserve-fund amendments required to implement the policy; and
THAT the proposed policy include a provision for Council approval and public notice before the sale, conversion or material encumbrance of municipal parkland, consideration of replacement land and service impacts, and reinvestment of net disposition or land-right proceeds for parkland and recreation purposes.
