 12.1
Thomas MacMillan, Clear Lane
 Clear Lane resident, Thomas MacMillan, requests that Council consider initiating a grant-funded Two-Zone Floodplain Management Feasibility Study along the Moira River corridor and Stoco Lake, incorporating the Province's pre-paid 2022 airborne LiDAR elevation dataset, 100% federally subsidized scoping through Climate Ready Infrastructure Service (CRIS), and 90% grant funding through the Federation of Canadian Municipalities (GMF Adaptation in Action stream, active intake closing December 15, 2026).  His formal submission package with attachments are included with this agenda item.
12.2
Lager Dawgs Hockey Tournament
 John Dyks, on behalf of the Lager Dawgs hockey team, requests a Letter of Municipal Significance for a liquor sales licence for the Lager Dawgs hockey tournament to be held at the Tweed arena on Saturday, January 23rd, 2027. The team also requests Council support for the rental of the ice for the tournament to be at the non-prime rental rate.
12.3
Bill 140, the Building Ontario Faster Act, 2026
 Mayor DeMarsh attended a briefing session regarding Bill140, the Building Ontario Faster Act, 2026, during which information was provided on the proposed amendments under Schedule 7 that would remove municipal approval authority for new landfill projects. Following the briefing, Mayor DeMarsh prepared a letter to Premier Ford outlining concerns regarding the proposed changes and their potential impact on municipal decision-making and local communities, attached.
