HOME
 Council is commencing hybrid meetings where some members will be present in Council Chambers, at the Recreation Hall and some via virtual means. Public may participate in person or are welcome to attend virtually.

We are pleased to advise that the location of Council Meetings have been moved to the Tyendinaga Township Recreation Hall at 363 McFarlane Road, Shannonville to provide extra space and allow the public to attend meetings in person. To provide accessibility to all, the Township will continue to allow the Public to attend live Council, Public and Committee meetings via “Zoom” video conferencing. Instructions for attending a meeting via Zoom are provided below.

How do I join a meeting via Zoom Video Conferencing?
Please visit: https://zoom.us/ and either sign-up for a free Zoom account or continue as a guest.

Download the Zoom software on your personal computer, or download the mobile app to your smart phone or tablet. 

Pre-registration is required, however, you will be required to provide your name and email address when attending the meeting virtually.
Please click the link below to register for the meeting: 
www.tyendinagatownship.com/meeting-registrations 

How can I provide Public Comment on Zoom?
At the Public Hearing: an opportunity for Public input will be provided at the end of the Public Hearing. Please ensure that you register indicating that you wish to speak at the Public Meeting. 
At the Regular Council Meeting: Please note that Regular Council Meetings and Special Council Meetings do not allow for an open question period. You will be able to attend virtually, however you will not be able to turn your camera or microphone on. 

Please Note: We encourage those wishing to view the meeting to also download the agenda, as it will not be displayed during the streaming process.

We strive to ensure that all documents on this site are accessible for people with disabilities, however, this is an on-going process and third party documents and information may not be accessible. If you require information in an alternate format, please call 613.396.1944. We will work with you to understand your specific information and accessibility needs and to provide for them within a reasonable time frame.
