PUBLIC WORKS
The Public Works Department builds, operates, maintains and repairs the County road network consisting of 561 two-lane kilometres of roads and 1 four-lane kilometre of road and 77 bridge and culvert structures with spans greater than three metres. The Department also manages three patrol yards, three gravel pits, and two office buildings. The public works fleet includes approximately 40 vehicles including light and heavy trucks, heavy equipment, trailers and various tools and equipment. The Department is organized into four divisions:
• Operations
• Construction
• Administration
• Fleet and Equipment
Public Works - 25 Nov 2026
Public Works - 28 Oct 2026
Public Works - 23 Sep 2026
CORPORATE SERVICES
The Corporate Services Department provides a diverse range of services primarily to the Corporation as a whole and to the departments within the Corporation. Support and expertise are provided in areas such as Information Technology, Finance, Legal, Human Resources Management, Records Management, Purchasing, Risk and Insurance Management, Realty Services, Communications, Printing, Photocopying and Mail Distribution. The Department is organized into five (5) divisions:
CAO's Office
Clerk's Office
Finance Department
Human Resources Department
Information Technology Department
