 8.
REPORTS FROM DEPARTMENTS
 8.1
CAO
 8.1.1
CAO 2026-19 Oxford County Archives Assessment Review (Presentation) 
 RECOMMENDATIONS:
That Oxford County Council receive Report CAO 2026-19 entitled “Oxford County Archives Assessment Review” and the Archival Assessment Review Report – Oxford County Archives (Attachment 1), prepared by Heritage Professionals;
And further, that County Council endorse staff to proceed with implementation of several recommendations noted in the Report including:
Oxford County Archives Mandate review and formation of a Collection Policy, Digitization Strategy, and Emergency Response Plan;
Creation of a Comprehensive Archives’ Holdings Inventory, as generally outlined in the Clerk’s Office Business Plan;
Processing of archival backlog received from Area Municipalities, Archives of Ontario and the public;
And further, that Archives staff work with Public Works to consider possible space options to accommodate the Archives current holdings and future accruals for the next 20+ years which will be brought back to Council as a future report and budget approvals.
8.1.2
CAO 2026-20 Proposed Actions to Address Landfill Capacity
 RECOMMENDATION:
That Oxford County Council receive the submission comments in response to ERO 026-1056 as detailed in Report CAO 2026-20, as information.
8.2
FINANCIAL SERVICES
 8.2.1
FS 2026-25 2027 Oxford County Library Business Plan and Budget
 RECOMMENDATION:
That the Oxford County Library Board’s October 20, 2026 recommendation to approve the draft 2027 Oxford County Library Business Plan and Budget, including a revised levy of $6,660,767 reflecting updated interdepartmental allocations, be referred to 2027 budget deliberations.
8.2.2
FS 2026-26 2027 Court Security Grant Special Tax Levy
 RECOMMENDATION:
That a special 2027 tax levy for a Court Security Grant for Woodstock Police Services in the amount of $81,332, determined on the same basis as the 2018 to 2026 annual special tax levies, be considered during 2027 budget deliberations.
8.2.3
FS 2026-27 2027 Water and Wastewater Rates
 RECOMMENDATIONS:
That Report FS 2026-27 presenting preliminary 2027 Water and Wastewater Rates for the County systems, be received and considered during the 2027 budget deliberations;
And further, that the amendments to Water and Wastewater Rates Policy 6.22, , in Attachment 1 to Report FS 2026-27 be approved.
8.2.4
FS 2026-29 OILC Debenture Issues – Oxford, Woodstock and Blandford-Blenheim
 RECOMMENDATIONS:
That By-Law 6896-2026, being a by-law to authorize the borrowing by issuing debentures, for a term of 20 years, in the amount of $541,883, for the purposes of the County of Oxford, be presented to Council for enactment;
And further, that By-Law 6897-2026, being a by-law to authorize the borrowing by issuing debentures, for a term of 10 years, in the amount of $2,529,000, for the purposes of the County of Oxford, be presented to Council for enactment;
And further, that By-Law 6898-2026, being a by-law to authorize the borrowing by issuing debentures, for a term of 15 years, in the amount of $2,500,000.00, for the purposes of the City of Woodstock, be presented to Council for enactment;
And further, that By-Law 6899-2026, being a by-law to authorize the borrowing by issuing debentures, for a term of 10 years, in the amount of $200,000.00, for the purposes of the City of Woodstock, be presented to Council for enactment;
And further, that By-Law 6900-2026, being a by-law to authorize the borrowing by issuing debentures, for a term of 10 years, in the amount of $3,000,000.00, for the purposes of the Township of Blandford-Blenheim, be presented to Council for enactment.
8.2.5
FS 2026-24 2027 Business Plans and Budget
 RECOMMENDATION:
That the 2027 Draft Business Plans and Budget be received for discussion purposes.
8.3
WOODINGFORD LODGE
 8.3.1
WDFL 2026-05 Long-Term Care Committee of Management Quarterly Report November 2026 Q3
 RECOMMENDATION:
That Oxford County receives the Committee of Management Updates from Woodingford Lodge for information, as per requirements under the Fixing Long-Term Care Act (FLTCA), 2021, Section 135.
