home owner attempted to turn the bus where child is and it won’t work in winter, spoke 
with home owner who was doing it and working on it – agreement at some point. 
 
- D. Alguire – veterans cross walk in contact with company and will be 2nd or 3rd week of 
September – let office know in advance for street closure and notifications. 
 
- T. Evans – paperwork filled out for JBC flooring request should be in for next month’s 
Lions meeting. 
 
R. Layng – any concerns or issues over bingo machine with JBC/PAC – no shows since – 
JBC have not met since approval was given, so they are not yet aware. - T. Evans - on 
behalf of J. Smid and I thank you very much and it’s working very well. 
 
DELEGATION(S) 
- None - 
 
PAYMENT OF ACCOUNTS 
MOVED BY T. EVANS 
SECONDED BY R. LAYNG 
THAT Council approve the accounts for payment as circulated.                                 CARRIED 
 
 

 
2
REPORTS OF MUNICIPAL OFFICERS 
- Admin. Assistant – YTD Building report  
 
- CAO - YTD vs 2026 budget – G. Kearney - word is out in the community that we aren’t 
planning for the future and we have low reserves – wanted to make note that we are sitting 
with over $800,000 in reserves and that is still with having to use or transfer out in 2026 
approx. $378,000 for the arena condenser and the Fire Dept. tanker, so for a small 
Municipality I think that’s pretty great. 
 
- CAO – the final disbursement of bequeath to the Township and to the Fire Dept., from 
the estate of the late George Ivan Pike has been received - $3582.20 each.  Donations have 
been received as follows:  Mayor Scott $100.00 towards the Centre 76- 50th celebration 
and Councillor Alguire $500 towards the remembrance crosswalk. 
 
- CAO - We have a resident who is territory sales manager for a company that does 
curbside and transfer site refuse collection and is inquiring about being given the 
opportunity to submit a proposal for this service for the Township – everyone agrees and 
contact will be made with current collector requesting a proposal prior to end of contract 
for Council discussion. 
 
- CAO – Current Council upcoming regular meeting schedule is October 13th and 
November 9th – the current term ends November 14th and the new term starts November 
15th with the inaugural and first meeting to be held November 16th.  Current council agrees 
their last meeting will be October 13th and there shouldn’t be a need for the November 9th 
meeting. 
 
- Dept. of Public Works – capital service quote – will cover the 95m to do drainage from 
Mill St. to Sarah St., had not put in for a capital project, however would like permission to 
transfer from operating budget to cover this cost and have it completed - $30,371.00 – there 
is an additional cost for another 20m $6,394.00, but do not feel that is necessary at this 
point and may not have the funds – 50 year life expectancy 
MOVED BY M. SMITH 
SECONDED BY R. LAYNG 
THAT Council approve the request of the Director of Public Works to move certain 
surplus budgeted operational funs to a capital expenditure for drainage works from Mill St. 
to Sarah St.  Capital expenditure shall equal transferred budgeted funds and is not an 
increase in overall expenses.  
 
 
 
 
 
     CARRIED 
 
- Dept. of Public Works - Continue to work on the Asset management update – 40-50% 
complete. 
 
- Dept. of Public Works - will get camera and check the other 20m and see what if 
anything needs to be done there right now, at a county meeting this week brought up what 
we are looking at doing and trying to see if we can work with the county because a lot of 
county storm drains are through ours and intertwine and connected as well and work with 
them.  
 
- H. Scott – Mapleview have some artifacts to donate – given the fact our heritage is full 
and some can’t be displayed the County is also contacting other committees in Leeds and 
Grenville and see if they want anything, there will be some coming to Athens.  
 
CORRESPONDENCE 
– Novatech – recommendation to update zoning bylaw – 3 (County) amendments. 
MOVED BY M. SMITH 
SECONDED BY T. EVANS 
THAT Council approve recommendation of Novatech Engineering to have three 
amendments consolidated into the Township’s Zoning Bylaw. 
 
     CARRIED 
  
- D. Johnson – request for any amount to waive, donate or reduce ice rental rate for 
Women’s 3 on 3 hockey tournament fundraiser for palliative care – 8 hour rental – Saturday 
September 26th – Council unanimously agreed to reduce the rental rate 50%. 
  
- AMCTO – recognition of D. Noonan 35-year membership milestone. 
 

 
3
- Bill Thake award  
MOVED BY T. EVANS 
SECONDED BY M. SMITH 
THAT Council endorse and support the nomination of William (Billy) Dixie Jr. for the 
2026 Bill Thake Memorial Award for Economic Development Leadership.      CARRIED 
 
 COMMITTEE REPORTS 
Centre ’76 - 50Th ad hoc – a draft sign has been proposed with betty signs – incorporated 
old rink with new with the lettering blue 48 x 60 – approx. $700.00 plus HST. - request for 
committee for anniversary, financial support, approval of fire hall for future meetings, 
removal of bulletin board, approval for free public skating and the sign placement, paint 
the wall will need to be all white – use of the tv for slide show what has been gathered - to 
clarify about governance vs operation - what is needed to be approved by Council – 
everything.  - Mayor Scott has resigned from the Committee. 
 
- T. Evans – JBC - September 27th – euchre tournament and raise funds and cut the costs 
of the event.  -  D. Noonan - put out for us a gmail account of past experiences at the rink 
and incorporate in our slide show and E. Earl has provided some information the museum 
has and asking for donations and other than that – not sure what financial support we will 
need – mainly the sign and refreshments. 
MOVED BY G. KEARNEY 
SECONDED BY A. DANCY 
THAT Council approve the purchase of a 50th celebration plaque for Centre ’76, as 
presented by the ad hoc committee, Council also approves expenditures for refreshments 
for the event.  
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
     CARRIED 
  
PLANNING 
MOVED BY D. ALGUIRE 
SECONDED BY A. DANCY 
THAT Council approve consent application B-51-26 – Raats – 72 County Road 5, South. 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
     CARRIED 
BY-LAWS 
MOVED BY A. DANCY 
SECONDED BY G. KEARNEY 
THAT Council introduce and read a first and second time bylaws to provide for advance 
votes to be held prior to voting day, to allocate 2026 budgeted revenue to reserves, to 
transfer funds from reserves and reserve funds, to authorize the execution of an agreement 
for Centre ’76 canteen services and to provide for reduced hours of voting in institutions 
and retirement homes. 
 
 
 
 
 
 
     CARRIED 
 
MOVED BY G. KEARNEY 
SECONDED BY A. DANCY 
THAT Council read a third time bylaws to provide for advance votes to be held prior to 
voting day, to allocate 2026 budgeted revenue to reserves, to transfer funds from reserves 
and reserve funds, to authorize the execution of an agreement for Centre ’76 canteen 
services and to provide for reduced hours of voting in institutions and retirement homes.  
Signed by the Mayor and the Clerk and numbered 2026-19, 2026-20, 2026-21, 2026-22, 
2026-23. 
 
 
 
       
 
     
 
 
     CARRIED 
 
PUBLIC QUESTION PERIOD 
- E. Earl – McAvoy Road and digging and lots for sale – no signage – 3 approved 
severances – they can post for sale however they like. 
 
- M. Rusland - glad to see dead trees at Elbe Cemetery cut down.  
 
QUERIES AND COMMENTS BY COUNCIL 
- C. Fenlong – approached about making Wiltse to George from Elgin a one way street 
only during school year – a lot more to it than that and did speak to principal the way it is 
setup now they feel it  is 100% better – don’t know if it will come back to look at further  
– did tell her and talked to D. Howard  and didn’t have an issue with buses using George 
St. that’s where the problem was. 
  
 

 
4
- R. Layng – regarding Farmersville and observations, power at the pavilion seems to be 
ongoing problem and condition of the washroom the hand dryer was broke off the wall and 
would be nice to clean up the washrooms and get it painted - I know people are in and out 
or who or what but for weekends like Farmersville, it should be more presentable and 
cleaned up – C. Fenlong - it was painted last year and within a month you wouldn’t know 
it had been done – also a few years ago at Lions request  a panel was put on the outside of 
the rink for use for Farmersville and now everything has moved to pavilion/canteen area 
and that’s not used and the panel at pavilion not meant for that much use and it’s 
overloaded. 
- R. Layng - New condenser – annual maintenance requirements and warranty set? in and 
all good - yes 
 
- M. Smith - backhoe running and useful? - C. Fenlong – yes, used several times -  8th line 
and transfer site and beavers. 
 
- T. Evans – new condenser and ice falling from roof in winter – looking at installing a 
heat tracer on roof.  
- T. Evans - Inspection forms – C. Fenlong – yes, using what you gave me, office staff 
revamped.  – T. Evans - asked could you put the backhoe report in with time sheets and 
documented weekly? –– time stamped photos maybe as well, start a job and finish a job 
both you and A. Sargent. 
 
- G. Kearney –– speed signs? – C. Fenlong - already sent somewhere else, going to try to 
pull two for next year – can keep replacing batteries in them but two months they last, need 
to take them down. 
 
- A. Dancy - nothing  
 
- D. Alguire – let everyone know I’m removing my name from the 2026 election –a lot 
going on.   – H. Scott - will you please see the crosswalk project through to the end – D. 
Alguire - absolutely and everyone will have the information I do and proceed forward when 
done.  D. Noonan advised looking into logistics as withdraw date from candidacy has 
passed and name is already on the ballots; it will remain as is. 
 
- D. Noonan – nothing 
 
- H. Scott – Mapleview – 3 weeks ago tomorrow watched as they moved 60 residents 
George and I on hand – honour to be there.  - As of 14th of August, had 283 on waiting list  
took those 60 in and then took 13 from Brockville hospital, 2 from Kingston, 1 from Perth 
and 1 from Ottawa – finished with list of people in crisis – been operating under 
construction funding, took out a mortgage for building it is setup so when new mortgage 
kicks in no increase in county taxes.  
- H. Scott - Ross Nichols needed $40 for insurance for candidate meeting so I gave him 
$20 for half. 
- H. Scott - At ball field the building used by Horse A Rama – I offered T. Scott and I 
would supply paint for the building – the building is supposed to be taken home, can we 
let it stay there and put a stone base under it to set it on and their group would paint it?  
– M. Smith - it’s not in the way.  – G. Kearney - it’s grown from the time when they started 
– not in the way.  – D. Alguire - when brought it in, it was an annual proposal – in spring 
out in fall and not stay there permanently – H. Scott - will make it look better – D. Alguire 
- is ok if it’s not in the way remaining – H. Scott - can we give them a load of stone if they 
need it to sit it on – everyone agrees it can remain, paint and stone. 
- H. Scott – to C. Fenlong - can someone trim the cedars, near his place, can’t see the 
formerly Farmersville sign – C. Fenlong - our plan was to take it all out – the cedars are 
over grown and take them out and put two small ones in - they are in the hydro lines almost. 
- H. Scott – T. Scott and I working on cemetery and T. Evans came and cut the trees and 
won’t take too much before it can be mowed by the caretaker and will be great to have it 
done. 
- Thank you everyone for coming. 
 
 
 
 
 

 
