8. REPORTS FROM MUNICIPAL OFFICERS 
8.1. 
Clerk’s Report 
The Clerk provided updates regarding the Sovereign Road Waste Disposal Site expansion, 
AMCTO Zone 9 activities, summer student funding opportunities, the municipal road tour, Pokki 
Road Bridge repairs, Briggs Pit matters, and other ongoing administrative projects. Council 
discussed project priorities and directed Administration to continue pursuing funding 
opportunities and required approvals where appropriate. Council also expressed support for 
submitting applications for available 2027 summer student funding programs. 
 
8.2. 
Treasurer’s Report 
The Treasurer reported on conference attendance, outdoor rink board delivery and installation, 
ROMA conference planning, grant applications, and current financial and administrative matters. 
Council discussed future equipment and capital replacement planning. 
 
HR Assistant joined the meeting at 6:33 p.m. 
 
8.3. 
Public Works Report 
The Public Works Manager reviewed ongoing road maintenance activities, including gravelling, 
grading, brushing operations, roadside maintenance, and culvert replacements. The Public 
Works Manager advised that the Township's 1988 combination plow/sander truck required 
significant repairs and was not considered economically viable to return to service. Council 
discussed the operational impacts of removing the vehicle from service, replacement options, 
and associated costs, noting that future equipment replacement requirements would need to be 
considered through the Township's capital and budget planning process. 
 
Public Works Manager left the meeting at 6:55 p.m. 
 
8.4. 
Fire Chief’s Report 
The Fire Chief reviewed recent departmental activities, emergency responses, training 
initiatives, wildfire preparedness activities, and regional fire service meetings. The Fire Chief 
provided updates regarding volunteer recruitment, departmental staffing, professional 
development opportunities, and ongoing administrative improvements within the department. 
Council was advised of challenges related to emergency water supply, tanker capacity, mutual 
aid requirements, and winter access to the fire hall, as well as the future replacement needs of 
4

aging fire apparatus. Council discussed emergency preparedness priorities, operational 
requirements, water supply options, and long-term capital planning for fire service equipment. 
 
8.5. 
Council Member Reports 
Mayor Maxwell reported on meetings and municipal activities attended on behalf of the 
Township since the previous Council meeting, including participation in the municipal road tour 
and attendance at the September 2026 Lakehead Rural Municipal Committee meeting. Mayor 
Maxwell advised that the Committee was not expected to meet again until January 2027. 
 
Councillor Halvorsen reported that the next OPP Detachment Board meeting was scheduled for 
October 15, 2026, and advised that no Lakehead Rural Municipal Committee meeting had 
recently been held. 
 
Councillor Maxwell provided comments regarding the municipal road tour and advised that the 
Thunder Bay District Municipal League meeting was currently on hold pending the municipal 
election cycle and year-end scheduling. 
 
8.6. 
Other Agencies’ Reports 
Council reviewed correspondence and reports received from other agencies as listed in the 
Clerk’s Report, which were received for information. 
 
