Council’s direction. 
 
CARRIED 
 
9. NEW BUSINESS 
9.1 Municipal Alcohol Policy Review – Bring-Your-Own-Event Permit 
Council reviewed the policy and discussed potential liability, administrative requirements, and 
enforcement considerations associated with Bring-Your-Own-Event permits. Following 
discussion, Council directed that the Municipal Alcohol Policy remain unchanged at this time 
and that Bring-Your-Own-Event permits not be permitted under the Township's current policy 
framework. 
 
9.2 Winter Operations and Preparedness 
Council reviewed winter preparedness measures, including road maintenance priorities, 
emergency access considerations, fire hall accessibility, rink flooding operations, and available 
water sources. Administration was directed to continue reviewing options related to winter 
maintenance, fire hall accessibility, emergency water supply, and operational preparedness, and 
to report back to Council with recommendations. 
 
Mayor Maxwell left the meeting at 7:46 p.m. Due to the loss of quorum, no business was 
conducted during her absence. 
Mayor Maxwell rejoined the meeting at 7:48 p.m. 
 
 
 
9.3 Pokki Road Bridge Repairs – Tender Award 
5

Council reviewed the tender results and discussed continued access requirements for affected 
residents, emergency vehicles, school transportation, and ongoing logging operations. Council 
expressed support for proceeding with the project provided that acceptable arrangements for 
access during construction could be confirmed. 
 
RESOLUTION 2026-185 
Moved by: Councillor Maxwell 
Seconded by: Councillor Halvorsen 
BE IT RESOLVED THAT Council approve the award of the Pokki Road Bridge Repairs contract 
to J & A Contracting (Thunder Bay) Ltd., including the provisional rock-fill item, for a total 
contract value of $16,192.00 plus HST; AND THAT the award be finalized once Administration 
has confirmed acceptable arrangements for continued residential and emergency access during 
construction; AND THAT the Mayor and Clerk be authorized to execute any agreements 
necessary to complete the project. 
 
CARRIED 
 
9.4 Sovereign Road Waste Disposal Site Expansion – North Rock Environmental Proposal 
Council reviewed the proposal from North Rock Environmental Inc. for hydrogeological and 
environmental services required to support the proposed expansion of the Sovereign Road 
Waste Disposal Site. Council supported proceeding with the time-sensitive drilling and 
monitoring work funded from landfill reserve funds. 
 
RESOLUTION 2026-186 
Moved by: Councillor Halvorsen 
Seconded by: Councillor Maxwell 
BE IT RESOLVED THAT Council accept the proposal from North Rock Environmental Inc. in the 
amount of $44,010.00 plus HST for hydrogeological and environmental services related to the 
Sovereign Road Waste Disposal Site expansion; AND THAT funding be drawn from the landfill 
reserve; AND THAT the Mayor and Clerk be authorized to execute any agreements necessary 
to complete the work. 
CARRIED 
 
10. BY-LAWS 
No bylaws were presented for consideration. 
 
11. CORRESPONDENCE 
Council reviewed correspondence from the Township of Puslinch regarding the Aggregate 
Resources Act and the importation, processing and blending of aggregate materials, as well as 
correspondence from the City of Port Colborne regarding sustainable and predictable operating 
funding for Ontario public libraries. Council received the correspondence for information. 
 
12. UPCOMING MEETING DATES 
Council reviewed the list of upcoming meeting dates. No changes were proposed.  
 
Fire Chief and Deputy Clerk/Treasurer left the meeting at 8:20 p.m. 
Council stood the meeting down for a break 
Council resumed at 8:24 p.m. 
 
 
 
