The Corporation of the Township of Conmee 
Administrative Report 
 
 
Date:  
 
November 10, 2026 
 
To:   
 
 
Mayor and Council 
 
Subject: 
  
Administrative Activity Report 
 
File Number:  
01-C10-0000 Administrative Activity Reports 
 
Submitted by:   
Karen Paisley Clerk 
 
 
RECOMMENDATION: 
THAT the Clerk's Report dated November 10, 2026, be received; and THAT Council provide 
direction as necessary. 
 
BACKGROUND: 
The purpose of this report is to provide Council with updates on administrative activities, 
ongoing projects, regulatory matters, and other items of municipal interest since the previous 
Clerk's Report. 
 
DISCUSSION: 
Pokki Road Bridge Rehabilitation 
Administration has confirmed with the consulting engineer that tender addenda omitted from 
the original tender package included provisions to maintain resident and emergency vehicle 
access throughout construction. The updated addenda was circulated to Council by email. 
Letters have been issued to affected property owners advising of the construction schedule. 
Notices have also been published on the Township website and through the municipal 
newsletter. Construction is currently scheduled to occur between November 16 and November 
22, 2026. 
 
Hume Road Landfill Closure Plan 
Administration has authorized North Rock Engineering Inc. to submit the finalized Hume Road 
Landfill Closure Plan to the Ministry of the Environment, Conservation and Parks (MECP) for 
regulatory review and approval. The final report incorporates revisions discussed during recent 
meetings with Ministry staff, including updates to the post-closure monitoring and reporting 
program. Administration has also received a preliminary Class C construction cost estimate for 
the closure works. The estimated construction cost is approximately $440,000, excluding HST, 
and includes a contingency allowance. The consultant has advised that costs may be reduced if 
suitable cover material can be sourced locally. Following receipt of MECP approval, 
Administration will return to Council with recommendations respecting project delivery, 
procurement options, construction scheduling, and funding considerations. 
 
 
 
12

Sovereign Road Waste Disposal Site Expansion 
Administration continues to work with North Rock Engineering Inc. regarding the proposed 
expansion of the Sovereign Road Waste Disposal Site. North Rock has advised that the test 
pitting program has been completed and access trails required to support the project have 
been established. Installation of six additional groundwater monitoring wells is scheduled to 
commence on November 16, 2026. Following installation, the wells will be developed, tested 
and sampled as part of the hydrogeological assessment process. Over the winter months, 
Administration and North Rock Engineering will continue preparation of the hydrogeological 
assessment, Design, Operations and Closure Plan, and Environmental Compliance Approval 
amendment application required to support the proposed landfill expansion. Any future landfill 
expansion work will be subject to separate Council consideration, regulatory approvals, and 
applicable procurement requirements. 
 
Emergency Management 
Administration has reviewed correspondence from the Ministry of Emergency Preparedness 
and Response advising of updates to the Alert Ready Broadcast Immediate Event List (item 8.7-
11 - Other Agency Reports), which took effect October 8, 2026. The updates include additional 
alert categories and revised criteria for several existing emergency alert event types. 
Administration has reviewed the changes and has not identified any immediate amendments 
required to the Township's Emergency Response Plan at this time. The information will be 
considered during the next review of emergency communications procedures by the 
