7.8   Wahkohtowin requesting permission hosts a biochar burn on October 21st at  
40 Pine Street 
 
 
WHEREAS Wahkohtowin Development GP Inc. has requested permission to hold an 
educational biochar burn on Wednesday, October 21, 2026, during daytime hours, at 40 
Pine Street, Chapleau, which falls outside the scope of the Township’s municipal burn 
permit; 
NOW THEREFORE BE IT RESOLVED THAT the Council of the Corporation of the 
Township of Chapleau hereby approves the request of Wahkohtowin Development GP 
Inc. to conduct a biochar burn in a contained metal kiln on Wednesday, October 21, 
2026, at 40 Pine Street, at the location identified in the materials submitted, subject to the 
following conditions: 
1. The Chapleau Fire Chief, or designate, be notified in advance and may impose 
any additional conditions or cancel the burn if weather, wind or fire conditions are 
unsafe; 
2. The burns take place during daylight hours only and will be attended by a 
responsible adult at all times until the fire is fully extinguished; 
3. Adequate fire suppression equipment, including a charged water source or 
extinguishers, be kept on site for the duration of the burn; 
4. Only clean, untreated wood be burned; 
5. Members of the public attending the event be kept at a safe distance from the kiln; 
and 
6. Wahkohtowin Development GP Inc. assume all responsibility and liability for the 
burn. 
Carried. 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
