Page 3 of 17

The Public Works portion of $227,978.79 exceeds the $100,000 patching budget in the Public Works 
Reserve Fund. Four projects in the 2026 budget will not be completed this year, and their unspent 
funding would otherwise be returned to the Public Works Reserve at year end. Instead of drawing the 
difference from the reserve, the Treasurer, the Public Works Manager and the CAO recommend 
reallocating that 2026 funding to the asphalt repairs: 
Public Works Funding Source 
Amount 
Public Works Reserve Fund patching budget 
$100,000.00 
Reallocate 2026 Sidewalk Replacement funding 
$80,000.00 
Reallocate 2026 Storage Building Roofing funding 
$20,000.00 
Reallocate 2026 Sea Can Dome funding 
$13,000.00 
Reallocate a portion of 2026 Bridge Maintenance funding 
$15,000.00 
Total available 
$228,000.00 
This funds the Public Works portion in full, with a balance of $21.21 remaining. 
Amendment to Budget: The low tender exceeds the $100,000 estimate approved in the 2026 budget for 
asphalt patching. Under the Township's budget policy, this report and the agenda notation serve as 
notice of an amendment to the 2026 budget. 
Recommendation
BE IT RESOLVED THAT Council award RFT 2026-10-PW-01 Asphalt Repairs to Pioneer Construction 
Inc. of Sault Ste. Marie, Ontario, in the amount of $252,702.33 plus applicable HST; 
AND FURTHER THAT the total net cost of $257,149.89, including the Township's net share of HST, be 
funded as follows: $10,974.78 from the Water Reserve Fund; $18,196.32 from the Sewer Reserve 
Fund; and $227,978.79 from the Public Works Reserve Fund patching budget of $100,000.00 
together with the reallocation of 2026 funding from Sidewalk Replacement ($80,000.00), Storage 
Building Roofing ($20,000.00), Sea Can Dome ($13,000.00) and a portion of Bridge Maintenance 
($15,000.00); 
AND FURTHER THAT the Chief Administrative Officer be authorized to issue the purchase order to 
Pioneer Construction Inc. 
