Flows at the Wetlands were highest during the first few days of July before decreasing and 
stabilizing at approximately 1,100 to 1,500 m³/day for the rest of the month. Although influent 
and effluent flows frequently exceeded the facility's rated capacity (1,063 m³/day), all recorded 
flows remained well below the peak design capacity (4,475 m³/day). 
Figure 1 compares the influent and effluent flows to the system’s rated capacity and peak flow 
design limit.    
 
 
Figure 1: Cobalt Wetlands Influent and Effluent Flows – July 2026 
 
The Cobalt Wetlands experienced relatively stable flows during winter before heavy rains and 
snow melt in April caused influent flows to reach approximately 9,000 m³/day and effluent 
flows to peak at approximately 12,400 m³/day. 
 
Following this event, flows gradually declined through May, June, and July, stabilizing closer to 
normal operating conditions.  
 
