ENNISKILLEN,custom_html_pdf,https://www.enniskillen.ca/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Minutes-Council-October-19-2026.pdf,"THE CORPORATION OF THE TOWNSHIP OF ENNISKILLEN 
 
SEVENTEENTH MEETING 
 
   MINUTES  
           OCTOBER 19 2026 
 
 A meeting of the Council of the Township of Enniskillen was held on Monday 
October 19 2026 at 4:30 pm at the Enniskillen Council Chambers. 
 
Pecuniary Interest 
Mayor Marriott opened the meeting and requested that each member of Council declare 
an interest at the appropriate time within the agenda where an interest may exist. 
 
A. Minutes 
 
Moved by Councillor Krall 
Seconded by Councillor Van Dun 
That the minutes of the meeting of October 5 2026 be adopted as circulated. 
Carried. 
 
B. Interviews 
 
1. Drainage 
4:30 pm - Meeting to Consider Revised Henderson Oriet Drainage 
Report 
 
Moved by Councillor Krall 
Seconded by Councillor Williams 
That the meeting to consider the Revised Henderson Oriet Drainage 
Report be opened. 
Carried. 
 
Present: R. Dobbin Engineering Inc. – David Moores, Ray Dobbin 
Landowners present: Tony and Jane Straatman, Wendy Stevens, Shirley 
Scott 
 
Tony Straatman did not agree with the drainage area on the new report. The 
Engineer confirmed that the new proposed drainage area was used for 
calculations and to complete the report. Tony Straatman and Wendy Stevens 
were questioning the size of the proposed culverts (Culverts #3, 5 and 6) and 
why the work had to be completed. It was explained that Shirley Scott’s 
culvert (Culvert #4) was installed as an emergency replacement. The old 
1990’s reports do not address culverts.  
 
 
 
 

SEVENTEENTH MEETING 
 
    
2 
 
     OCTOBER 19 2026 
 
 
Moved by Councillor Van Dun 
Seconded by Councillor Williams 
That the Revised Henderson Oriet Drainage Report be accepted. 
Motion failed. 
 
The discussion was opened back up by the Chair. 
 
It was noted that the original Section 74 and Section 78 requests for cleaning 
and culvert replacements were submitted by Tony Straatman in June and 
October of 2024 which Council and the Engineer are responding to. It was 
explained that if there is no interest at this time to replace the culverts at Tony 
Straatman and Wendy Stevens properties (Culverts #3, 5 and 6) and Council 
was satisfied with this for the time being, the report could be referred back to 
the Engineer to modify with the removal of these culvert replacements for the 
time being. The culverts would be added as future work so that when the 
culverts fail in the future, provisions would be in the report for their 
replacement.  
 
Moved by Councillor Krall 
Seconded by Councillor Williams 
That the report for the Revised Henderson Oriet Drain be referred back to the  
Engineer to remove the replacement of Culverts #3, 5 and 6 but the report  
will be modified to include provisions for future replacement. 
Carried. 
 
The Meeting to Consider the Revised Henderson Oriet Drain was closed and  
regular Council resumed. 
 
Request received from Duncan Graham for brushing and beaver dam 
removal on the Stonehouse Drain. 
 
Moved by Councillor Krall 
Seconded by Councillor Burke 
That Councillor Van Dun be appointed Council Representative and a site 
meeting be scheduled for the Stonehouse Drain. 
Carried. 
 
 
 
 
 
 

SEVENTEENTH MEETING 
 
    
3 
 
     OCTOBER 19 2026 
 
 
2.  
5:00 pm - Delegation Request – Dave Hendeson, Lambton County International  
Plowing Match 2027 
 
Dave Henderson was recently selected to lead the 2027 International Plowing 
Match set to take place at the farm of Clayton and Linda McLauchlin on Petrolia 
Line. Dave provided an overview of what to expect in the near future. Needs 
such as water, road closures, dust control, Fire, EMS and OPP were presented. 
 
Dave Henderson requested a representative from the Township be appointed as 
the main contact to work with Dave and his group on keeping communications 
open between all involved. Councillor Krall volunteered to be this person, at no 
cost to the Township. 
 
Moved by Councillor Williams 
Seconded by Councillor Van Dun 
That Councillor Krall be appointed the Township of Enniskillen representative for 
the 2027 International Plowing Match. 
Carried. 
 
5:15 pm – Public Works Superintendent Darcy Mitchell attended the meeting to 
provide Council with an update on the Public Works Department. 
 
Construction on the Black Creek Bridge on Marthaville Road is progressing on 
schedule. The new mower is in service as of late September. Public works staff 
are scheduled for grader and snow plow training in the near future. The parks are 
going to be winterized in the next week. Trucks are getting ready to go for winter 
maintenance. Hydrant flushing is complete, some valve exercising is complete, 
Oil Springs and Dawn Euphemia meter calibrations are finished and Petrolia 
meter calibration will be completed soon.  
 
Moved by Councillor Williams 
Seconded by Councillor Burke 
That the Case IH MD 83 Disc Mower purchased in 2023 be declared surplus to 
the Township and that the Public Works Superintendent be permitted to sell as he 
sees appropriate.  
Carried.  
 
C. 
Correspondence for information  
 
Moved by Councillor Krall 
Seconded by Councillor Williams 
That Correspondence items #1 – 4 be Received and Filed. 
Carried. 

 
SEVENTEENTH MEETING 
 
    
4 
 
     OCTOBER 19 2026 
 
D. Correspondence requiring motions 
 
Moved by Councillor Van Dun 
Seconded by Councillor Williams 
That the Resolution from the Township of Ramara requesting that Transport 
Canada Review and Amend the Water Aerodrome Public Consultation 
Requirements be Received and Filed. 
Carried. 
 
Moved by Councillor Krall 
Seconded by Councillor Van Dun 
That the resolution from the Township of Ramara requesting Support for 
Enhanced Municipal and Watershed Representation in the Proposed Regional 
Conservation Authority Governance Framework be Supported. 
Carried. 
 
Moved by Councillor Krall 
Seconded by Councillor Burke 
That the Request from the Lambton County Music Festival for 2027 Financial 
Support be referred to 2027 budget discussions. 
Carried. 
 
E. Accounts 
 
Moved by Councillor Krall 
Seconded by Councillor Burke 
That the accounts be paid as circulated. 
Cheque #20573 – 20588  $24,890.12. 
Carried. 
 
F. Other Business 
 
1.  Moved by Councillor Williams 
     Seconded by Councillor Van Dun 
     That the 2026 Municipal Election Accessibility Plan be accepted as presented. 
     Carried. 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 

 
