Dog Tags 2027
Open Session RePort
Background:
The municipality issues dog tags yearly to its ratepayers for various prices/fees
depending on the sex of the dog and how many dogs one owns. This is a very
time consuming and manual process. Administration would like to streamline
the process making the use of staff time more efficient and effective.
Comments:
Staff propose that the township simplify the dog tag process moving fonruard in
2027 and beyond.
Propose we charge a standard fee of $35/dog.
During 2027 we will include a new dog tag for each animal which will be a lifetime
tag. lf-an animal loses its tag another one can be purchased for a fee of $20'00.
ln 2028 and future years we will simply issue an invoice for the renewal of the
dog tag(no new tag will be needed). lt will be up to the owner to advise Township
statf it tfrey no longer own an animal or if they have gotten a new animal.
January of each year we will invoice the owners of the dogs and have a due
date of February 26,2027. After that time, all amounts owning will be transferred
to the taxes with a $50.00 administration fee (current process)'
lf the dog owner is a tenant, the land owner will be consulted prior to the dog
tag being placed on the owner's tax roll (current process).

,}
€
;
Recommendation:
That the Council of Dawn Euphemia supports Administration's
recommendation to change the process of dog tags and fees for the year
2027 and future years.

