OPEN SESSION REPORT
Background:
The purpose of this report is to update the Shetland Park Seasonal & Transient Camper
Handbook / Code of Conduct Rules and make rules and regulations that need to be
followed while staying at the Campground.
Discussion:
We have had a few issues with our previous campground rules and regulations. Staff
reviewed various campground rules and would like to implement the new rules and
regulations for the 2027 camping season.
This will give Campground staff a clearer understanding and hopefully make their job
supervising the park less stressful.
Staff will be redesigning the Camp Ground Reservation forms for the various types of
camping. (seasonal, monthly, weekly, transient and group camping')
Financial lmplications:
I am proposing we raise the 2027 Camping fees by 3%'
RECOMMENDATION:
That Gouncil approve the Seasonal & Transient Camper Handbook/Code of Gonduct
tor 2027 as weil as the Golf Gart Rules and approve a 3o/o increase to the 2027
Gamping fees.

Seasonal & Transient Camper Handbook/Code
of Conduct
The rules in the Camper Handbook/Code of Conduct are intended to promote safety and to make the
camping experience a pleasant one for you and your neighbour's. lf you do not understand any rule,
please discuss it with Campground Management. Violation of a specific rule which management, at its
discretion, determines to be detrimentalto the Campground, its staff, or its other guests may result in
sanctions. Possible sanctions include, but are not limited to, temporary loss of camping privileges,
termination of the Seasonal & Transient Camper Rental Contract, and immediate expulsion from the
Campground.
please take time to review this Handbook/Code of Conduct, ask questions if you need clarification, and
do your best to be a good neighbour.
By placing my signature on this Facility Rental Contract, I agree on behalf of myself and my guests to
abide by all the rules and regulations as set out in this document by the Corporation of the Township of
Dawn Euphemia. I also take full responsibility for any damage done to campground property or private
property by myself and/or my guests and/or my pets and agree to cover any costs incurred. I also agree
on behalf of myself and my guests, that the Corporation of the Township shall not be held responsible for
theft of property or property damage as a result of fire, vandalism, acts of God, or the actions of other
campers.
