OPEN SESSION REPORT
Background:
The pirpose of this report is to provide Council with an update on the progress of the Asset
Management Plan and financial strategy.
Under Ontario Regulation 588/17, municipalities must report to Council at least once per
year on the current progress of the Asset Management Plan and any barriers aligning
operations with the pian. A full update of the plan will be required after 5 years. (2030).
Discussion:
Ontario municipalities must comply with Ontario Regulation 588/17 Asset Management
planning for Municipal lnfrastructure. The Requirements of the Regulation were phased
in as follows:
October 2016
June 30, 2019
June 30, 2025
Approved Asset Management Report from BM Ross
Approved Asset Management PolicY
Received BM Ross Asset Management Report 2025
lncluding levels of service.
The AMP work that might be under taken for 2027 includes the following
Road network condition assessments
Bridge and culvert insPections

Relation to Strategic Plan/Other Plans:
This report is to measure the actions of the Township to those prescribed by the AMP
measuring progress in implementation while identifying any factors impeding the
Townships' ability to implement our asset management. Any such impeding factors should
be accompanied with a strategy to address those factors.
Financial lmplications:
O. Reg 588/17 requires a 10 year capital plan that forecasts the costs of implementing the
lifecycle management strategy and the lifecycle activities identified in the AMP. The
Financing Strategy developed as part of the 2025 AMP includes a 10 year forecast period
to enable the Township to evaluate the sustainability of its assets throughout this period.
The AMP Financing Strategy has identified a funding gap of $816,786 annually. To
address this gap, the Township is working at developing means to grow revenue sources
both in the short-term and long-term as costs continue to increase.
Yearly review of the Asset Management plan will occur at budget time starting in 2027 .

