Good day, 
I am reaching out to you as the Advisor for Zones 1 and 1A on behalf of the Inspectorate of Policing. 
Now that the municipal elections have been completed, your Police Service Board membership 
may have changed. There are many things to consider. 
 The current composition of your Board remains intact until the Council(s) make new 
appointments, up to six months. This applies to both elected appointees and community 
members. 
 Provincial appointees are not impacted by the municipal election and remain until their 
appointment expires 
 I am aware that many Detachment Boards still have vacancies, and I continue to raise this 
issue within the Inspectorate. 
 All new appointees must complete the Roles and Responsibilities training before taking 
their seat at the Board table.  
 All new appointees will have six months to complete the Thematic Training. 
 I recommend that appointees take screenshots of their training completion to ensure they 
have proof of completion. 
 New Appointees can contact the Ontario Police College to register  
OPC.Registrar@ontario.ca 
 
 Once all appointments have been completed, please send me a list of your entire board 
membership 
