S. Trivers welcomed the Board of Health members, read the land acknowledgment, took roll call, and asked for declarations of 
Luc Morrissette
Dr. John Tuinema - Associate Medical Officer of Health & 
Director of Health Protection
Suzanne Trivers - Board Chair
Kristy Harper - Director of Health Promotion & Chief Nursing Officer
Jody Wildman - 1st Vice-Chair
Rick Webb - Director of Corporate Services
THAT the Board of Health agenda dated June 24, 2026, be approved as presented.
Comprehensive Health Promotion in Action: 
• Nurturing Algoma
• Planet Youth
An overview of comprehensive health promotion at Algoma Public Health was provided by the Healthy Growth & Development 
and the School Health & Community Wellness programs, with a focus on two initiatives: Nurturing Algoma and Planet Youth 
Algoma. The alignment of initiatives with strategic directions and Ontario Public Health Standards was highlighted and the 
importance of upstream approaches and community partnerships for improving population health outcomes was emphasized. 
The Nurturing Algoma initiative was described as a collaborative action project focused on early childhood mental health, 
developmental screening, and building local data infrastructure for a developmental profile of children aged zero to six in 
Algoma. The Planet Youth Algoma initiative is a community-based, long-term upstream prevention approach targeting youth 
substance use, grounded in the Icelandic Prevention Model. The PowerPoint presentation was included in the Board of Health 
Agenda Package.
Discussion took place and questions were answered to the Board's satisfaction.
