Dr. Loo spoke to the alPHa/COMOH meeting she and Dr. Tuinema attended in June. She reported that, following a resolution 
passed by the APH Board of Health at its February meeting to improve the Hepatitis B immunization schedule, a resolution 
titled Strengthening Hepatitis B Prevention in Ontario Through Vaccination in the First Year of Life  was presented jointly by 
Algoma Public Health and Simcoe Muskoka District Health Unit at the alPHa Annual General Meeting and passed.  Work 
continues in order to bring the changes into effect, and Board of Health will be updated on progress. 
The APH employee appreciation day held May 29 was well received. Highlights included a guest speaker presentation on the 
ethical use of AI in public health as well as a presentation to staff of our new strategic plan.  
The leadership team participated in a strategic planning retreat to review strategic pillars, goals, actions and resource 
alignment. This was a positive step in agency strategy development. 
The 2025 annual report was included in the agenda package in both English and, for the first time, French. Electronic copies can 
be accessed on the APH website and printed copies are available as well.
As part of its commitment to Truth and Reconciliation, Algoma Public Health has installed the Maamwesying Ontario Health 
Team's declaration of values in all APH office locations. A flag-raising ceremony was held on site in honour of Indigenous History 
month, with Indigenous partners/guest participating, presenting, singing and sharing. 
The Board was informed of the addition of a hybrid vehicle to the fleet for cost savings.
Dr. Loo announced the upcoming retirement of Rick Webb, Director of Corporate Services. 
RESOLUTION
