Re: ADSAB 2026-2036 Housing and Homelessness Plan – Public Engagement 
Opportunities 
Dear Mayor Nantel and Members of Council: 
The Algoma District Services Administration Board (ADSAB) is developing a new 
10-year Housing and Homelessness Plan for 2026-2036. This correspondence is being
provided to Council for information and to request assistance in promoting upcoming public
engagement opportunities to residents of your community.
Why is ADSAB Developing a New Plan? 
As a designated Service Manager, ADSAB is required under Ontario’s Housing Services Act, 
2011 to maintain a Housing and Homelessness Plan for the communities it serves. ADSAB’s 
existing 10-Year Housing and Homelessness Plan, Opening Doors to Better Lives, was 
developed in 2013 and has reached the end of its 10-year planning period. 
Since the existing plan was developed, the housing and homelessness landscape has 
changed considerably. Housing affordability pressures have intensified, homelessness has 
become more visible, community needs have evolved, and the policy and service-delivery 
environment has changed. 
The new 2026-2036 Housing and Homelessness Plan will provide a long-term strategic 
framework to help inform ADSAB’s housing and homelessness planning and priorities over the 
next decade. The Plan will be one of several tools used to support decision-making, 
recognizing that future initiatives and investments will also be influenced by factors such as 
available funding and resources, feasibility, partnerships, emerging community needs, and 
provincial and federal policies and programs.  
How Will the New Plan Be Developed? 
ADSAB has retained OrgCode Consulting Inc. to support the development of the new plan. 
The process will consider a range of information, including local housing and homelessness 
data, demographic and economic trends, existing policies and programs, future needs, and 
information gathered through community and stakeholder engagement. 

This work will provide an updated understanding of housing and homelessness across the 
District to support the development of the 2026-2036 Housing and Homelessness Plan. The 
consultant’s proposed approach similarly combines quantitative evidence and engagement 
information in developing the Plan. 
Public Participation and Community Engagement 
As part of this work, ADSAB and OrgCode will be seeking information from residents and 
communities across the District through a District-Wide Housing and Homelessness Survey 
and a series of public engagement meetings. These opportunities will provide additional local 
information and perspectives to complement the other data and research being considered. 
District-Wide Housing and Homelessness Survey 
Residents, service users, service providers and other community members are invited to share 
their perspective on housing and homelessness through the District-Wide Survey. The online 
format will help reach participants through ADSAB’s large and geographically dispersed 
service area. The survey is consistent with OrgCode’s proposed district-wide engagement 
approach. 
Survey Opens: September 28th, 2026 
Survey Closes: October 31st, 2026 
English Survey: https://adsab.link/hhp-survey  
French Survey: https://adsab.link/plli-sondage 
Public Engagement Meetings 
In addition to the survey, ADSAB and OrgCode will host three-in person public engagement 
meetings and one-virtual meeting. These sessions will provide an opportunity to hear directly 
from residents about housing and homelessness within their communities. 
The following public engagement meetings have been scheduled: 
City of Elliot Lake 
Wednesday, October 28th, 2026 
5:30 p.m. – 7:00 p.m. 
Collins Hall 
120 Hillside Dr. N. 
Elliot Lake, ON 
Town of Blind River 
Tuesday, October 27th, 2026 
5:30 p.m. – 7:00 p.m. 
Blind River Community Centre 
110 Indiana Ave.,  
Blind River, ON 
Municipality of Wawa 
Thursday, October 29th, 2026 
5:30 p.m. – 7:00 p.m. 
Michipicoten Memorial Community Centre 
3 Chris Simon Dr. 
Wawa, ON 
Virtual Public Engagement Meeting 
Tuesday, November 10th, 2026 
6:00 p.m. to 7:30 p.m. 
Microsoft Teams 
Link Available at: 
https://adsab.link/hhp 

Residents are welcome to complete the District-Wide Survey, attend a public engagement 
meeting, or participate through both opportunities. 
Additional information about the project, including the survey and public engagement 
opportunities, will also be available through ADSAB’s dedicated project webpage: 
English Webpage: https://adsab.link/hhp 
French Webpage: https://adsab.link/plli  
Request for Municipal Assistance 
Given the size and geographic diversity of the Algoma District, assistance from member 
municipalities will help ensure residents across the District are aware of these opportunities. 
ADSAB respectfully requests Council’s assistance in promoting the District-Wide Housing and 
Homelessness Survey and upcoming public engagement meetings within your community. 
To assist with this effort, a Public Engagement Notice is enclosed with this correspondence 
and may be shared directly with residents through municipal websites, social media, 
newsletters, community notice boards and other appropriate communication channels. For 
convenience, electronic copies can be provided upon request by contacting info@adsab.on.ca. 
Thank you for your assistance in helping ADSAB reach residents throughout your community. 
Sincerely, 
Jordan Kemp 
Director of Housing Services 
Algoma District Services Administration Board 

