Report Title: 2026 Christmas Holiday Schedule 
 
Purpose: To obtain Council approval for the proposed 2026 Christmas and New Year 
holiday schedule for the Municipal Complex/Office, Municipal Landfill Site, commercial 
and residential garbage collection, and other municipal operations. 
 
Background: Each year, Administration develops a Christmas holiday schedule for 
Council’s consideration and approval. The schedule is intended to provide employees with 
appropriate time off during the holiday season while ensuring that essential municipal 
services continue to be provided to the community. 
 
The proposed schedule covers the weeks of December 21 to 26, 2026, and December 28, 
2026, to January 2, 2027.  
 
Analysis/Discussion: For the week of December 21 to 26, 2026, Administration 
recommends the following: 
 
- 
The Municipal Complex/Office will be open to the public Monday through 
Wednesday and closed Thursday and Friday. 
- 
The Municipal Landfill Site will be closed Friday and Saturday only. 
- 
Commercial garbage collection will take place on Monday and Wednesday only. 
- 
Residential garbage collection will remain unchanged and will take place on 
Wednesday. 
 
For the week of December 28, 2026, to January 2, 2027, Administration recommends the 
following: 
 
- 
The Municipal Complex/Office will be closed to the public Monday through Friday. 
Municipal 
Council Report 

- 
The Municipal Landfill Site will be closed on Friday only. 
- 
Commercial garbage collection will take place on Monday and Wednesday only. 
- 
Residential garbage collection will remain unchanged and will take place on 
Wednesday. 
 
The public will be advised in advance of all holiday-related changes affecting municipal 
services, departments, facilities, and operating hours. 
 
For employees whose scheduled days off are not recognized statutory holidays, vacation 
time or accumulated time in lieu will be used, or employees may be required to work 
depending on individual circumstances and the need to maintain uninterrupted municipal 
services. 
 
A separate holiday operating schedule will be developed for the Eddy K. Lefrançois 
Recreation Centre based on employee availability, statutory holidays, regular user-group 
requirements, and any special ice-rental requests. This schedule will be communicated 
publicly closer to the holiday period once user-group requirements are known. 
 
Funding: N/A 
 
Financial Implications: No signiﬁcant additional ﬁnancial implications are anticipated. 
Employee scheduling will be managed in accordance with applicable employment 
agreements, statutory holiday requirements, vacation entitlements, accumulated time in 
lieu, and operational requirements. 
 
Recommendation: Whereas the Council of the Corporation of the Township of 
Dubreuilville hereby: 
 
1. Approves the 2026 Christmas and New Year holiday schedule for the Municipal 
Complex/Office, Municipal Landﬁll Site, and municipal garbage collection services 
as presented in this report. 
2. Authorizes the Municipal Complex/Office to be open to the public Monday through 
Wednesday and closed Thursday and Friday during the week of December 21 to 25, 
2026. 
3. Authorizes the Municipal Complex/Office to be closed to the public from Monday, 
December 28, 2026, through Friday, January 1, 2027. 
4. Approves the Municipal Landﬁll Site and garbage collection schedules as outlined in 
