KILLALOE HAGARTY AND RICHARDS,custom_html_pdf,https://www.killaloe-hagarty-richards.ca/sites/25/files/2026-11/November%203%202026%20Regular%20Meeting%20Minutes_0.pdf,"November 3, 2026 
Regular Meeting 
7:00 PM 
Council for the Township of Killaloe, Hagarty and Richards met on the above date with Mayor 
David Mayville and Councillors Harold Lavigne, Bil Smith, Maureen MacMillan, Ted Browne, 
Carl Kuehl, and Brian Pecoskie in attendance. 
Call to Order: 
Mayor Mayville chaired the meeting which he opened and called to order. 
Mayor Mayville advised that there is an addition to the agenda under “Unfinished Business” 
– Legacy Benches 
Moved by Harold Lavigne 
Seconded by Maureen MacMillan 
BE IT RESOLVED, that Council for the Township of Killaloe, Hagarty and Richards hereby 
adopts the agenda for the Regular Council meeting of November 3, 2026, as presented.    
Carried. 
First Nations Land Acknowledgement: 
First Nations Land Acknowledgement read by Mayor Mayville. 
Moment of Silent Reflection: 
Mayor Mayville requested a moment of silent reflection. 
Mayors Address: 
Mayor Mayville congratulated Councillors Pecoskie, MacMillan and Smith on their re-election, 
thanked Councillors Lavigne, Kuehl and Browne for their service and dedication to the 
Township, and welcomed incoming Councillors Kuiack, Poulton, Gavin and McFalls.  Mayor 
Mayville provided an overview of the election results, including voter turnout statistics and 
the outcomes of the referendum questions.  Mayor Mayville reported on his attendance at 
a County Council meeting, which included meetings of the Development and Property 
Committee and the Operations Committee.  Mayor Mayville advised that an ad hoc Housing 
Task Force Committee has been established to develop Terms of Reference and identify 
additional members to be invited to participate in discussions regarding the Renfrew County 
Housing Corporation’s property tax exemption proposal.  Mayor Mayville congratulated MPP 
Billy Denault on his appointment as Parliamentary Assistant to the Minister of Municipal 
Affairs and Housing, Rob Flack.  Mayor Mayville advised that the Municipal Accountability 
Act will come into effect on November 15, 2026, introducing a standardized municipal Code 
of Conduct, changes to the municipal Integrity Commissioner process, and new and 
expanded education and training requirements for members of Council.  Lastly, Mayor 
Mayville provided an update on the 2027 OPP Annual Billing Statement, noting that the 
increase is capped at 11% over the amount payable in 2026. The total amount payable for 
2027 is $615,291, representing an increase of $60,975 from the previous year. 
Pecuniary/Financial Interest: 
No pecuniary/financial interest was declared. 
Minutes: 
Moved by Ted Browne 
Seconded by Maureen MacMillan 
Motion to approve the minutes of the Public Meeting and Regular Council meeting of October 
20, 2026 open sessions.    Carried. 
Correspondence: 
Township of South Algonquin – Re: Urgent Request Employment Services Relief – 
Moved by Bil Smith 
Seconded by Harold Lavigne 
THAT Council for the Township of Killaloe, Hagarty and Richards hereby supports and 
endorses the resolution adopted by the Township of South Algonquin at its Regular Council 

meeting held on April 1, 2026, requesting temporary employment insurance relief for 
seasonal workers for the 2026-2027 off-season, which is attached; 
AND FURTHER THAT this resolution be forwarded to MP Cheryl Gallant, the Minister of Jobs 
and Families, MP – Nipissing – Timiskaming Pauline Rochefort, Acting Commissioner for 
Workers, Canada Employment Insurance Commission Chris Roberts, MPP Billy Denault, 
Ontario Ministry of the Environment, Conservation and Parks, Ontario Ministry of Labour, 
Immigration, Training and Skills Development, Ontario Ministry of Tourism, Culture and 
Gaming, Ontario Parks – Algonquin Provincial Park Superintendent, Federation of Northern 
Ontario Municipalities, Association of Municipalities of Ontario, Tourism Industry Association 
of Ontario and all Ontario municipalities for their support and endorsement.    Carried. 
Town of Gananoque – Re: Request for Endorsement – Declaration Against Religious 
Violence –  
Moved by Bil Smith 
Seconded by Maureen MacMillan 
THAT Council for the Township of Killaloe, Hagarty and Richards hereby supports and 
endorses the declaration against religious violence adopted by the Town of Gananoque at 
its Regular Council meeting held on October 7, 2026, , which is attached; 
AND FURTHER THAT this resolution be forwarded to the Town of Gananoque, Mayor John 
S. Beddows for the Town of Gananoque, Minister Grahm McGregor; Minister of Citizenship 
and Multiculturalism of the Province of Ontario and all Ontario municipalities.    Carried. 
Mayor Mayville – Re: County of Renfrew 2026 Levy Summary Report – filed 
RCDHU – Re: RCDHU Launches New Five-Year Strategic Plan: Forward Together – filed 
Councillor Smith – Re: Request to Reopen a ServiceOntario Centre in Killaloe –  
Moved by Harold Lavigne 
Seconded by Maureen MacMillan 
THAT Council for the Township of Killaloe, Hagarty and Richards hereby supports and 
endorses the letter received requesting to reopen a ServiceOntario Centre in Killaloe, 
Ontario, which is attached; 
AND FURTHER THAT this resolution be forwarded to MPP Billy Denault, and Renfrew County 
municipalities including the County of Renfrew.    Carried. 
Killaloe & Area Lions Club – Re: Support for Annual Santa Claus Parade – Council 
acknowledged that this support had been included in the approved budget, and the letter 
was considered received and then filed. 
County of Renfrew – Re: Council and Committee Monthly Summary October 2026 – 
filed 
MVACL – Re: Invitation to their Respite Home Open House - filed 
Unfinished Business: 
CAO/Clerk Gorgerat presented the proposed holiday closure schedule, which was approved 
by Council. The Municipal Office and Public Works Department will be closed from December 
25, 2026, to January 4, 2027, while the Waste Department will be closed from December 
25, 2026, to January 2, 2027. 
CAO/Clerk Gorgerat provided Council with correspondence received from the Integrity 
Commissioner, the Township Solicitor and the County of Renfrew regarding the recovery of 
human resources costs associated with the Mayor obtaining legal advice on Strong Mayor 
Powers. Council was asked to review the information and provide direction regarding the 
outstanding invoices submitted by the County of Renfrew.  Council directed that the 
outstanding invoices be paid and that staff develop a policy to establish a clear process for 
obtaining and paying for legal or professional advice to prevent similar issues from arising 

in the future. Council further advised that they did not wish to receive the emails offered by 
the County of Renfrew. 
Councillor MacMillan provided background information and an update on the Legacy 
Benches, advising that the benches have been installed by the Public Works Department 
and commended staff for the installment. Councillor MacMillan also identified the locations 
of the benches throughout the Township and advised that arrangements will be coordinated 
with the five families for an official dedication and opening ceremony. 
New Business: 
Mayor Mayville and Councillors Browne, Kuehl and Lavigne provided farewell remarks, 
reflecting on their time serving on Council and expressing their appreciation for the 
opportunity to serve the Township and its residents and acknowledged staff for their hard 
work and dedication. 
Confirming By-Law: 
Moved by Ted Browne 
Seconded by Carl Kuehl 
THAT By-Law No. 60 – 2026 Being a by-law to confirm the proceedings of Council of the 
Township of Killaloe, Hagarty and Richards at its Regular Council meeting held on November 
3, 2026 be given its 1st, 2nd and 3rd reading and finally passed this 3rd day of November 
2026.    Carried. 
Adjournment 
Moved by Ted Browne 
Seconded by Carl Kuehl 
Motion to adjourn the Regular Council meeting held on November 3, 2026 for the Township 
of Killaloe, Hagarty and Richards.    Carried. 
