CAO/Clerk Gorgerat advised that staff continue to actively monitor the Ward 3 English Public 
ballot matter and have reached out to numerous individuals regarding ballots received and 
reported that to date, 111 of the 861 eligible voters have voted, and 136 individuals have 
been in contact with the Township, this contact includes both voters who have contacted 
the Township directly and individuals whom staff have reached out to as part of the ongoing 
follow-up process.  CAO/Clerk Gorgerat indicated staff continue to update the tracking list 
regularly to reflect additions, deletions, and any new ballots received and advised that staff 
have also conducted door-to-door visits and will continue these efforts as necessary to 
follow up with voters and address outstanding concerns.  CAO/Clerk Gorgerat reported that 
staff are focused on damage control and monitoring the situation as it develops and the 
next steps and the appropriate process moving forward cannot be determined until the 
results are finalized and the full extent of the situation is known.  CAO/Clerk Gorgerat also 
indicated that MMAH has advised that it does not have an established process in place to 
address circumstances of this nature and accordingly, once the results are available, staff 
will seek guidance from the Municipality’s legal counsel to determine the appropriate course 
of action and any necessary next steps if required. 
Mayor Mayville invited any Ward 3 candidates present in the gallery to address Council. 
Ms. Cate McFalls expressed concerns that staff had not done enough to reach Ward 3 
English Public voters. Councillor Browne disagreed with her concerns and shared his 
perspective on the matter.  Councillor Smith also shared his perspective on the matter. 
CAO/Clerk Gorgerat asked and received approval to defer the discussion regarding the 
Christmas Schedule. 
CAO/Clerk Gorgerat reported that three (3) properties are scheduled for tax sale on 
November 18, 2026, and are currently published in the two (2) local newspapers and online 
on Ontario Tax Sale for a 4-week period from October 14th to November 4th, 2026.  
CAO/Clerk Gorgerat advised that the combined minimum tender amount for all properties 
is $161,090.85 and interested purchasers must submit tenders in accordance with the 
requirements established under provincial legislation.  She also indicated that property 
owners retain the right to redeem their properties by paying all outstanding taxes, penalties, 
interest, water/sewage and any related costs up to the day the documents are filed. 
New Business: 
Councillor MacMillan asked and received approval to have the Municipal Office open for 
Halloween and an allocation of $100.00 for candy. 
