Mayors Address: 
Mayor Mayville reported that he attended a County Council meeting along with the 
Development and Property and Operations committees and he that he would be attending 
the first meeting of the Renfrew County Forest Sector Committee on October 7th.  Mayor 
Mayville advised that further discussions regarding the proposed property tax exemption 
would take place at the County level and noted that the primary objective was to achieve 
savings of approximately $126,000 in education tax costs for the County.  Mayor Mayville 
reported that he had not received any comments from Council regarding the standardized 
Code of Conduct legislation prior to the October 2nd deadline. And lastly, Mayor Mayville 
shared his views on the letter received from Minister Flack regarding the Buy Ontario Act, 
emphasizing the importance of adhering to the legislation as strongly as possible. 
