1. Planner Report 
 
Huron County Planner Laura Simpson called upon to present her report MV01-
2026. The purpose of this report is for two variances from the Howick Zoning By-
law to permit the construction of a detached garage to the east of the existing 
residence.  
This property is located at 2038 Martin street in Gorrie, zoned VR 1 and is 
designated settlement area and natural environment totaling 3.7 acres in size and 
contains a single detached residence.  
 
Drawings of the proposed garage were provided to Council attached to this report.  
During the circulation process there were no comments from members of the 
public or municipal staff. Maitland Valley Conservation did submit comments 
proposed structure will be situated in the flood fringe however the owners have 
been in touch with the Conservation Authority and have no concerns with the 
proposed location.  
 
It is recommended that minor variance application MV01-2026 be approved with 
the following conditions the applicants provide confirmation to the satisfaction of 
the Township that the lands acquired from the Township have merged on title. The 
structure be generally constructed as shown in the elevations and site plan and the 
variance approval is valid for a period of 18 months from the date of the 
Committee’s decision.  
 
 
