10.2.1 
DPS-2026-22, Used Pumper-Tanker Purchase 
 
Fire Chief/ Manager of Development and Protective Services 
called upon to present his report. Staff are requesting council 
receive this report for information and that council authorizes an 
additional $43,0000.00 be pulled from the Fire Reserve for the 
purchase of a 2018 Freightliner Fort Garry Pumper Tanker and 
provide direction to staff in regard to the retirement of 2-4.  
 
Council previously approved $300,000.00 to be pulled from the 
Fire Reserve for the purchase of a used pumper tanker that meet 
all our requirements. Staff explained that this one being proposed 
is being sold by a neighbouring municipality, meets a general 
scope of what we are looking for, well maintained and has all of 
its service records.  
 
Staff explained that there has been great difficulty trying to find 
anything in the $300,000.00 range to date that meets all of our 
requirements and still had a decent life expectancy. Fort Gerry 
does still manufacture this specific truck, and the body is built in 
Winnipeg.  
 
Additionally, staff are looking for direction from Council in regard 
to the disposal of the existing truck, staff suggested reproposing it 
in the joint Huron County Fire Training, sell the truck and put the 
money into the reserve and should Council wish to sell it staff are 
proposing to put a reserve bid of $20,000.00 on the truck.  
 
Two other municipalities have shares in the truck that staff are 
proposing, there must be approval from all municipalities involved 
before the deal is finalized. 
 
Moved by: Councillor Rognvaldson  
Seconded by: Councillor Grimes  
 
That the Council of the Township of Howick receive report DPS-
2026-22 for information purposes;  
 
And that Council authorize an additional $43,000.00 plus 
unrecoverable HST from the Fire Department Reserve for the 

