10.3 Manager of Public Works – Scott Price 
10.3.1 
PW-2026-19, Bowman Subdivision Winter Maintenance  
 
Manager of Public Works Scott Price called upon to present his 
report staff explained that there is no winter maintenance 
agreement in place for the Bowman Subdivision this season. 
Once Phase 1 is complete it is common for the Township to 
assume winter maintenance.  
 
Staff are proposing that we take on the winter maintenance at no 
cost to the developer. There will be one resident with occupancy 
very soon with the second not too far behind. Staff looked at our 
other shared road agreements in the Township and on average 
we were receiving about $2,200.00. It was discussed that a legal 
agreement will be drafted to maintain the roadway at the same 
level as our other roadways. Phase two requires the top lift of 
asphalt be completed before the roadway is assumed. It is 
anticipated it will be about three years before this happened.  
 
Moved by: Councillor Rognvaldson  
Seconded by: Deputy Reeve Gibson  
 
That Howick Council receives report PW-2026-19, Bowman 
Subdivision Winter Maintenance, for information; 
                 And that Council direct staff to prepare a Winter Maintenance 
Agreement between the Township of Howick and 2822071 
Ontario Ltd. for the provision of  winter maintenance services 
within the Bowman, effective November 1, 2026; 
 
And that the Winter Maintenance Agreement remain in effect on 
an interim basis until Phase Two of the Bowman Subdivision is 
completed and the applicable roads with the subdivision have 
been formally assumed by the Township of Howick  

