consideration. The Clerk-Treasurer reported on the next fire meeting, outstanding tax 
amount, application for NORDS Grant, as well as the Community Emergency 
Preparedness Grant, water tests were submitted for both halls with no issues 
identified, clarification from the School Board confirmed that McCrosson Tovell 
school is presently idled and not closed, presently awaiting pricing for the Bergland 
Hall kitchen remodeling, and the replacement defibrillator for the Morson Hall has 
been installed. Council discussed the issue of Daylight Savings Time with the desire 
to stay with Manitoba’s time zone. The propane tanks from the previous supplier are 
to be removed this week. Councillor Lundgren reported on recent Locum House 
meeting and an offer the purchase for one of the lots has been accepted. Council 
would prefer to have our share of the funds returned once the sale is completed.  
 
ADJOURN #26-73 PENTENY & LUNDGREN & CARRIED that the meeting be adjourned at 
9:32 p.m. and the meetings be moved back to Bergland Hall until further notice.  
 
 
Mayor 
 
Clerk",📄 Official Minutes,2026-11-23
