PRESENT Mayor C Fadden, Councillors: K Cottam, N Gate, W Lundgren, and B Pentney. Clerk-
Treasurer: P W Giles, Intern: D Swire, Rd Supt Jeffery Patterson, and E Pearson 
(retiring Rd Supt). Mayor Fadden thanked Ed Pearson for his 25 years of service and 
presented him with a retirement gift on behalf of council and rate payers.   
MINOR VARARIANCES 
The Clerk-Treasurer gave an overview first for the Hannam minor 
variance and once that was dealt with an overview of the Lehman minor variance 
application including a response from the Lake of the Woods Control Board with 
regards to compliance with the high-water mark elevation set back requirements. 
MINUTES  #26-56 LUNDGREN & PENTNEY & CARRIED that the minutes of the regular 
meeting of Council, held on August 4 2026, be approved as printed. 
ACCOUNTS #26-57 GATE & COTTAM & CARRIED that the accounts in the amount of  
$206,770.88 and representing disbursements for the month of August be approved for 
payment. 
 
BY-LAW 419 
#26-58 COTTAM & LUNNDGREN & CARRIED that By-law No 419, being 
the Rich & Lori Lehman Minor Variance By-law, be enacted. RECORDED VOTE 
for YEA: COTTAM, FADDEN, GATE, LUNDGREN. NAY: PENTNEY.  
 
