Road Superintendent Appointment by-law, be enacted.  
 
FURNACE     #26-60 GATE & LUNDGREN & CARRIED that due to the lapsing of the ten-year 
inspection of the fuel oil tank, council authorizes changing the heating system for 
Morson hall to propane. And further that we request proposals for the replacement of 
said furnace.  
 
PROPANE     #26-61 COTTAM & GATE & CARRIED that pursuant to quotes received for the 
supply of propane, council authorizes switching the supplier to Sarjeant Propane. 
Councillor PENTNEY declared an interest as his brother-in-law works for Sarjeant 
Propane.  
 
AED                #26-62 PENTNEY & GATE & CARRIED that pursuant to the quote received from 
Rescue 7, Council authorizes the purchase of one ZOL AED defibrillator and two 
ZOL AED Plus batteries. 
  
KIDS               #26-63 GATE & COTTAM & CARRIED that Council authorizes a donation of 
$100.00 in support of the Rainy River Recreation Kid’s Mini Fishing Derby.  
 
OTHER 
Pursuant to the recommendation of the interview committee, Council appointed 

Jeffery Patterson as Road Superintendent. The Road Superintendent reported on road 
work including mowing of Old Highway, gravelling preparation for surface treatment 
on Gate & Helder Rd W, brushing on Gerben & Helder Rd, replacement of culvert at 
Gov’t dock, repainting of stone cemetery sign at Morson Cemetery, removal of 
beaver damns, grinding down rock in roadways, and replacement of mower at the 
Morson Dump. The Clerk-Treasurer reported on the next fire meeting, outstanding 
tax amount, notification of Washagamis Bay First Nation Gardening Island Land 
Claim, OPP 2027 levies being capped at an 11% increase, need to replace oil tan kat 
Morson Hall, recognition of Clerk-Treasurer’s 45 years as a member of AMCTO. 
Municipal election results, all present members of council acclaimed to office. 
NWHU requires a updated water test for the Community Halls. Arrangements have 
been made for shredding of documents pursuant to document retention by-law. 
Council discussed interest in applying for a Community Emergency Preparedness 
Grant for a generator for Bergland Hall (the Emergency Reception Centre). 
Councillor PENTNEY provided a report on the Morson Hall and Firehall updates to 
bring propane services into compliance and other maintenance. Council discussed 
rate-payer inquiry regarding multiple RVs on residential lots and are awaiting further 
information from our consultant on the matter. Council received a thank you note 
from RRHS Chem-Free grads for their donation.  
 
