on July 7 2026, be approved as printed. 
ACCOUNTS #26-51 PENTNEY & COTTAM & CARRIED that the accounts in the amount of  
$119,445.82 and representing disbursements for the month of July be approved for payment and 
further that the total amount of June disbursements be amended to $147,513.04. 
 
OCIF 
#26-52 COTTAM & GATE & CARRIED that Council supports the following resolution: Township 
of North Stormont requesting the Province of Ontario to permanently double the Ontario 
Community Infrastructure Funding. 
 
LOCUM 
#26-53 GATE & COTTAM & CARRIED that pursuant to the recommendation of the Locum House 
Committee, Council agrees to the proposal to have our jointly owned 2 vacant lots appraised and 
offered for sale. 
 
LAME DUCK #26-54 GATE & COTTAM & CARRIED Whereas Section 275 of the Municipal Act, 2001 restricts 
certain expenditures and liabilities during a Lame Duck period; and whereas Council wishes to 
ensure the continued and orderly operation of the Township during such a period; therefore be it 
resolved that the Clerk-Treasurer is authorized to approve expenditures and incur liabilities on 
behalf of the township up to $25,000 per transaction, provided such expenditures are within the 
approved municipal budget and are otherwise permitted by law. And further, that any expenditures 
exceeding $25,000, unless otherwise authorized under the Municipal Act, 2001, shall require 
Council approval. 
 
OTHER 
The Road Supt was absent. The Clerk-Treasurer reported on the next fire meeting, a discussion with 
Canada Border Service regarding a visitor to Canada reporting system at Gov’t Dock, it was relayed 
that Council does not have any objection to the proposal, the land use permit for Carl’s Rd has been 
approved subject to receipt of payment, Revco had given a couple of possible designs for 
renovations of Bergland Hall kitchen, the taxes outstanding amount was given as well as the fact 
that six properties have been registered for tax sale, a thank you letter was received from R & G 
Armistead for road crew work to open Aksel Rd after the recent wind storm event. MTO is doing 
design work on Lathe Mill culverts (near public works garage on Hwy 600) replacement. Our group 
benefits portal was compromised and is now restored. Councillor Cottam relayed a concern about 
the rock area along the Gov’t Dock which the road crew will repair. A replacement defibrillator is 

being checked into for Morson Hall and a replacement battery for Bergland Hall. Applications are 
being received for a new Road Supt until Aug 19th 2026. Nominations are being filed for the 
upcoming municipal elections with nominations closing August 21 2026. 
 
ADJOURN #26-55 PENTNEY & COTTAM & CARRIED that the meeting be adjourned at 9:20 p.m.  
 
 
Mayor 
 
