OPP costs 
 
 
 
Resolution 26-184 :  Marc Dupuis – Steve Brousseau 
WHEREAS an increase of up to 11% in municipal policing 
costs represents a significant financial pressure for small and 
rural municipalities and ultimately places additional pressure 
on the municipal tax levy; 
NOW THEREFORE BE IT RESOLVED THAT Council for the 
Municipality of Mattice – Val Côté hereby support Resolution 
# RC26178 made by Council for the Municipality of Wawa, 
acknowledging the Province of Ontario’s action to limit the 
2027 OPP municipal policing cost increase to no more than 
11%, expressing concern that an increase of up to 11% in a 
single year remains significant for small, rural and northern 
municipalities and is not a sustainable long-term solution and 
requesting that the Province of Ontario establish a permanent, 
transparent and sustainable multi-year framework for OPP 
municipal policing costs that: a) includes a reasonable and 
predictable maximum annual increase in municipal OPP 
policing costs, taking into consideration municipal revenue 
growth, inflation, assessment growth, population growth, 
fiscal capacity and affordability impacts on local property 
taxpayers, including cost-of-living pressures; b) provides 
municipalities with a clear and itemized annual explanation of 
changes to their OPP policing costs, including, where 
applicable, changes attributable to staffing levels, salaries, 
benefits, 
calls 
for 
service, 
time 
standards, 
fleet, 
accommodation, support services, detachment administration 
and other provincial cost allocations; c) recognizes the limited 
fiscal capacity of small, rural, northern and OPP-policed 
municipalities and ensures that municipal policing cost 

October 20th, 2026 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
Meeting 26-12 
 
 
 
 
 
 
           Page 6 
 
 
increases do not disproportionately affect property taxpayers 
or compromise municipalities’ ability to deliver other essential 
services and infrastructures, and; d) recognizes that 
municipalities have limited ability to control policing costs 
arising from provincial legislation, regulation, staffing, 
compensation, collective bargaining, operational or policy 
decisions and provides appropriate provincial funding or cost-
sharing where significant policing cost pressures arise 
primarily from such provincial decisions, and; 
BE IT FURTHER RESOLVED THAT a copy of this resolution be 
forwarded to the Municipality of Wawa and to our local 
Parliament representatives, MPP Guy Bourgouin and MP 
Gaetan Malette. 
Carried 
 
 
