            Physician recruitment  
Resolution 26-154:  Marc Dupuis – Steve Brousseau 
WHEREAS municipalities have stepped in where they can but cannot 
continue to fund physician recruitment packages, housing incentives, 
locum coverage or clinic operations without dedicated provincial 
support. 
NOW THEREFORE BE IT RESOLVED THAT Council for the Municipality 
of Mattice – Val Côté hereby support the letter dated July 6th 2026 
sent to Premier Ford by the Mayor of the Town of Bruce Mines and 
requesting that the Province of Ontario establish a dedicated 
Northern Ontario Physician Recruitment and Retention Fund, 
accessible to small and rural municipalities, ensuring communities are 
not forced to subsidize provincial healthcare responsibilities, and that 
the Province work directly with northern municipalities to develop a 
coordinated strategy that reflects the unique demographic, 
geographic and fiscal realities of the North, and; 
BE IT FURTHER RESOLVED THAT a copy of this resolution be 
forwarded to the Town of Bruce Mines and to our local parliament 
representatives, MPP Guy Bourgouin and MP Gaetan Malette. 
Carried 
 
   
Salary disclosure 
 
Resolution 26-155:  Steve Brousseau – Marc Dupuis 
WHEREAS the Public Sector Salary Disclosure Act passed in 1996, 
requires that every public employer make available for inspection by 
the public, without charge, a written record of the amount of salary 
and benefits paid in the previous year by the employer to an employe 
to whom at least $100,000 in salary was paid, and; 
WHEREAS this $100,000 salary threshold has not been updated since 
1996 to reflect inflation; 
NOW THEREFORE BE IT RESOLVED THAT Council for the Municipality 
of Mattice – Val Côté hereby support the resolution made on May 11, 
2026 by Council for the Township of Clearview, requestion that the 
Public Sector Salary Disclosure Act be amended to reflect the impact 
of inflation on the $100,000 salary threshold for reporting, by either 
adding wording to reflect annual adjustments related to the consumer 
price index (CPI) or providing an adjusted salary of $200,000, and; 
BE IT FURTHER RESOLVED THAT a copy of this resolution be 
forwarded to the Township of Clearview and to our local parliament 
representatives, MPP Guy Bourgouin and MP Gaetan Malette. 
Carried 
 
 
Ontario Land Tribunal  
Resolution 26-156: Marc Dupuis – Joyce Malenfant 
WHEREAS the Ontario Land Tribunal (OLT) has the authority to 
overturn municipal planning decisions, often requiring municipalities 
to spend significant taxpayer dollars defending decisions that have 
already undergone a thorough local review process, and; 
WHEREAS local governments should have greater certainty and 
authority when decisions are consistent with approved Official Plans, 
provincial policies and sound planning principles. 

September 1st, 2026  
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
           Meeting 26-10 
 
 
 
 
 
 
         Page 10 
 
NOW THEREFORE BE IT RESOLVED THAT Council for the Municipality 
of Mattice – Val Côté hereby support Resolution no. 166-26 made by 
Council for the Town of Whitby, requesting that the Government of 
Ontario review the role and mandate of the OLT, to ensure greater 
respect for municipal planning decisions that are supported by 
evidence, public consultation and approved planning policies, and; 
BE IT FURTHER RESOLVED THAT the Province consider amendments 
to the Planning Act and the Ontario Land Tribunal Act to provide 
stronger deference to municipal decisions that align with provincial 
planning frameworks and Official Plans, and; 
BE IT FURTHER RESOLVED THAT the Province improve transparency 
and accountability withing the OLT by requiring clear and detailed 
reasoning when municipal decisions are overturned, and; 
BE IT FURTHER RESOLVED THAT the Province explore measures to 
reduce the financial burden on municipalities defending planning 
decisions before the OLT, helping to protect taxpayer dollars and 
improve the efficiency of the planning process, and; 
BE IT FURTHER RESOLVED THAT a copy of this resolution be 
forwarded to the Town of Whitby and to our local parliament 
representatives, MPP Guy Bourgouin and MP Gaetan Malette. 
Carried 
               
 
Funding public libraries 
Resolution 26-157:  Steve Brousseau – Joyce Malenfant 
WHEREAS public libraries provide essential services, including 
literacy, education, technology access, employment resources and 
community programming, and; 
WHEREAS the Ontario Library Association and Federation of Ontario 
Public Libraries have called for increased and sustainable provincial 
