MUSEUM
MUSEUM
Opened in November 2014, the Charlton Athletic Museum is a registered charity and a 
self-funded, volunteer initiative with a mission to preserve, present and promote the heritage 
of the club.
The museum – located in The Valley’s Covered End (or North Stand) – is run by a group of 
passionate, volunteer trustees, who dedicate their time to ﬁnding out more about the club’s 
illustrious history. Possessing an array of rare and sought-after artefacts and exhibits, the 
museum is a great way for supporters to learn about Charlton’s past.
Entry to the museum is free, though supporters are welcome to make a voluntary donation to 
the museum.
