Township of McNab/Braeside
Road Map
The Township is a rapidly growing community located amongst the
beauty of the Ottawa River, Madawaska River and White Lake.
Only a 30 minute drive from Kanata and Corel Centre, it offers the
convenience of city amenities for entertainment and business while
providing the residents with the peace and serenity of country life.
The historical and cultural background of the Township can be
viewed upon a visit to the Waba Cottage Museum and Gardens
located in the Village of White Lake.
Walking, cycling, cross-country skiing and snowmobiling can be
enjoyed on a recreational trail close to your own backyard. Also,
there is a ski resort just a few kilometers away at Calabogie Peaks.
There are two golf courses, beaches and four boat docks within the
Township boundaries. The Township has nine municipal parks with
recreation programs that include soccer, fast ball, and outdoor skating.
A variety of unique stores, restaurants, retail outlets, and other
businesses offer a selection of goods and services with a personal
touch that only small communities can offer. The industrial park
located near Hwy. 17 and the Town of Arnprior is an ideal location
for commercial and industrial enterprises to conduct business.
If you are visiting our Township, we welcome you and suggest you
visit the many beautiful areas within the Township of
McNab/Braeside.
