Item 7.B 
  
CORPORATION OF THE TOWNSHIP OF PELEE 
REPORT NO. 2026-62 
 
Author: 
Cathy Miller 
Report Date: 
October 14, 2026 
 
 
Mayor 
Date to Council: 
November 10, 2026 
 
To: 
Mayor and Members of Council 
 Subject: 
End of Term Report – Destination Development Committee 
 
 
Page 1 of 2 
Over this term, the Committee advanced discussions on tourism tax and str regulation 
matters, including Resolution 2024-DD09, receiving information regarding tourism 
taxation models, and Resolution 2025-DD07, supporting Council's consideration of a 
Municipal Accommodation Tax (MAT) as a tool to support tourism-related investment 
and promotion. 
 
The Committee also worked to improve the visitor experience through infrastructure and 
information initiatives. Resolution 2025-DD03 recommended funding for directional and 
wayfinding signage across the Island, while Resolution 2024-DD12 supported 
consideration of a digital visitor information and community engagement platform. 
These recommendations were in support of improved navigation, communication, and 
the overall visitor experience. 
 
Supporting local businesses remained a central focus throughout our work. Resolution 
2024-DD10 endorsed the creation of a Small Business Owner Toolkit through external 
grant funding, while Resolution 2024-DD13 established support for annual spring and 
fall business open houses to create opportunities for information sharing, networking, 
and business community building. Most recently, Resolution 2026-DD02 supported 
collaboration with the Leamington Chamber of Commerce through a joint networking 
event, further strengthening regional relationships with established, respected local 
funding and business planning agencies. 
 
The Committee also provided feedback on tourism marketing and destination 
promotion. Resolution 2026-DD03 recommended the production of the 2026 Island 
Brochure, and Resolution 2026-DD07 encouraged community engagement and 
promotion surrounding the Waterfront Trail Tour and visiting cyclists. 
 
Finally, recognizing the importance of long-term planning, Resolution 2026-DD06 
recommended that Council review the role and responsibilities of the Destination 
Development Committee for the 2026–2030 term absent a funding model to implement 
priorities identified within the 2021 Destination Development Implementation Plan. 
 
The Destination Development Committee provided a forum for collaboration between 
businesses, outside agencies like TWEPI, Leamington Chamber, Invest Windsor Essex, 
Regular Meeting of Council 
November 10, 2026 
Page 17 of 56

 
 
Page 2 of 2 
Business Development Bank of Canada, Community Futures, various lenders, The 
Waterfront Trail Trust and The Trans Canada Trail and Council, and consistently 
brought forward recommendations intended to strengthen responsible tourism, support 
economic development, enhance visitor experiences, and contribute to the long-term 
sustainability of Pelee Island. 
 
Thank you to members who gave their time sit this Committee",📄 Official Minutes,2026-11-23
