Minutes – September 17,  2026 
Present –Bill Harmon, Taylor Haskell, Eveline Maedel, Ron Cheetham, Anne-Marie Cartwright, 
Glena Clearwater 
 
Regrets – Phyllis Gauvin 
 
Additions to agenda: None 
 
Agenda approval - Motion by Glena Clearwater 2nd  Anne-Marie Cartwright Approved 
 
Previous Minutes: Motion:  by Ron Cheetham, 2nd Eveline Maedel that the minutes of June 
19, 2026 meeting be accepted as circulated.  Approved 
 
Business/Action Items arising from the Minutes:  
None 
 
PWS Update 
1. Cliffside Cemetery – Capacity Issues 
PWS & Senior Administrative Assistant to complete a review of the last 5 years of cemetery 
records regarding internments and lot purchases, to gain an accurate insight to determine an 
estimated number of years of useful life we have left in the current cemetery upon SAA return to 
office. 
2. The Cemetery By-Law Amendments & BAO Submission 
Following the completion of the mandatory 4-week public notification period, it is believed all 
legislative requirements under the Funeral, Burial and Cremation Services Act, 2002 have been 
met. The submission package delivered to the BAO licensing department included the draft by-
law amendments, photographic proof of the cemetery entrance postings, the local newspaper 
notice publication, and evidence of direct consultation with active monument suppliers. Staff will 
monitor the submission and provide a status update to the Committee once the BAO Registrar 
issues formal approval. 
 
3. Cemetery By Law – Related Forms 
30 relevant related forms have been developed by our SAA. We are still working to finalize the 
forms and process surrounding their implementation which will be completed prior to the by-law 
coming into effect.   
 
4. Cemetery Water Taps 
PW Crew has brought two taps above ground, two more still require raising which will occur this 
fall or in the spring of 2027.  
 
 
 
 

	  
	  
5. Other Items 
- Sanding of wooden garbage boxes has been added to the student’s summer to do list for 2027 
as we did not have time to complete this in 2026. 
- Request for additional flat marker/monument on lot prohibited in current by law - Rights Holder 
has been advised that the by law revision being worked on now would allow them to add a flat 
marker to an existing lot and PWS will reach out to her once by law is implemented. 
 
New Business 
• The committee would like to see the old sign at the beginning of Cemetery Road that 
provides direction to the cemetery replaced as it is peeling and fading. PWS will look into 
easement and any restrictions on putting up a sign there, as well as get quotes for 
replacement and/or street signage. 
 
• Historical Cemetery – a question was raised regarding clean up and tree removal and 
what the plans were.  PWS advised that as town employees currently are not chainsaw 
certified, then it would need to be contracted out. It is not known if there is room in the 
budget to start this work this year as approved budget numbers are not available yet. 
• A request to join the committee was received from Norm Sarrasin.  Motion: The 
committee recommends to Council that Norm Sarrasin be approved as member of the 
Cemetery Committee.  Motioned by G. Clearwater, Seconded by Ron Cheetham. 
 
The next meeting will be Thursday October 15, 2026 at 10:30. 
 
Meeting was adjourned on a motion by Ron Cheetham  at  10:50 
 
Recommendations to Council 
• The committee recommends that Council approve Norm Sarrasin as member of the 
Cemetery Committee.  Motioned by G. Clearwater, Seconded by Ron Cheetham. 
 
Summary of Action Items 
 
