A Briefing Note contains advice and/or recommendations from an employee, for council consideration. 
SUBMITTED BY Todd Francis – Interim Public Works Manager 
 
DATE November 17th, 2026 
 
BACKGROUND Schedule G of By-Law No. 28-2025 currently permits free residential 
dumping on the last Saturday of each month in addition to the spring and 
fall clean-up periods.  
Administration is recommending an amendment to remove the monthly 
free dumping days and retain only the spring and fall clean-up periods. 
 
 
 
ANALYSIS & 
DISCUSSION FOR 
COUNCIL 
CONSIDERATION 
The proposed amendment will reduce free residential dumping days from 
fourteen per year to four per year:  
Last Saturday of May,  
First Saturday of June,  
Last Saturday of September, and  
First Saturday of October.  
This change will reduce operational costs while continuing to provide 
seasonal disposal opportunities for residents.  
All current restrictions and tipping fees remain unchanged. 
 
RELEVANT POLICY 
AND/OR 
LEGISLATION 
Town of Moosonee By-Law No. 28-2025, Schedule G - Municipal Garbage 
Pick-Up Charges and Landfill Tipping Fees. Draft By-Law No. 18-2026 
amending Schedule G. 
 
FINANCIAL 
IMPLICATIONS 
The amendment is expected to reduce staffing and operating costs 
associated with weekend landfill openings and assist in preserving landfill 
capacity. 
 
ALIGN WITH COUNCIL 
STRATEGIC PLAN 
PRIORITIES 
 
Responsible Asset Management, Fiscal Responsibility, and Sustainable 
Landfill Operations. 
 
RECOMMENDATIONS  That Council approve the amendment to Schedule G of By-Law No. 28-2025 
and adopt By-Law No. 18-2026, reducing free residential dumping days to 
the spring and fall clean-up periods. 
 
 
BRIEFING NOTE 
Free Residential Dumping Days at the Municipal Landfill 
 

 
 
 
CAO’S COMMENTS 
AND/OR MOTION 
FOR COUNCIL 
CONSIDERATION 
BE IT RESOLVED THAT the Council of the Corporation of the Town of 
Moosonee approve the amendment to Schedule G of By-Law No. 28-2025  
and adopt By-Law No. 18-2026, establishing free residential dumping days 
on the last Saturday of May, first Saturday of June, last Saturday of 
September and first Saturday of October. 
 
 

  
 
 
 
 
 
