      BACKGROUND 
 
 
   
The CAO Work Plan identifies immediate operational priorities, strategic 
projects, corporate management initiatives, recruitment efforts, and major 
partnership files requiring administration attention.  
Due to ongoing staffing transitions, several Public Works responsibilities 
have been reassigned to the CAO for oversight and coordination. 
Key Work Plan Deliverables and Timelines 
• Immediate to Q4 2026: Water treatment agreement, legal matters 
briefing, airport leases, H-Block housing leases, recruitment initiatives, 
departmental reporting framework, and operational water/sewer risk 
management. 
 
• Q1 2027: Council Strategic Plan, Town Satisfaction Survey review, 
Economic Development Plan next steps, organizational review, MCFN 
governance committee framework. 
 
• Q2 2027: Official Community Plan approval process, housing and land 
development partnership advancement, staffing housing relocation 
planning. 
 
• 2027 Ongoing: Landfill partnership development, WAHA servicing 
obligations, records retention project, airport lighting funding strategy, 
policy implementation and corporate improvement initiatives. 
 
 
 
ANALYSIS & 
DISCUSSION FOR 
COUNCIL 
CONSIDERATION 
 
 
Administration is focused on five key areas:  
(1) water and wastewater sustainability and risk management,  
(2) WAHA-related agreements and infrastructure obligations,  
(3) housing and land development opportunities,  
(4) recruitment and organizational capacity, and  
(5) long-term strategic planning and governance initiatives.  
BRIEFING NOTE 
CAO Work Plan 
To Do List 

 Several operational risks require continued monitoring, while several 
strategic initiatives are targeted for Council consideration through 2027. 
 
 
 
 
RELEVANT POLICY 
AND/OR 
LEGISLATION 
 
 
 
Municipal Act, 2001; Town policies and procurement requirements; 
applicable environmental approvals; airport lease requirements; 
contractual obligations related to WAHA, housing, and infrastructure 
servicing. 
 
 
 
 
FINANCIAL 
IMPLICATIONS 
 
 
 
 
 
Several initiatives may result in future capital or operating budget impacts, 
including water and wastewater infrastructure, staffing housing, landfill 
development, airport improvements, and housing partnerships.  
Individual funding strategies and Council approvals will be brought forward 
as required. 
 
 
 
ALIGN WITH COUNCIL 
STRATEGIC PLAN 
PRIORITIES 
 
 
 
Supports infrastructure reliability, housing development, economic growth, 
Indigenous partnerships, organizational effectiveness, community 
sustainability, and long-term financial planning. 
 
  
 
 
RECOMMENDATION 
 
 
  
That Council receive this briefing note for information and acknowledge the 
CAO Work Plan priorities, timelines, and major corporate initiatives 
currently underway. 
 
 
 
CAO’S COMMENTS 
 AND/OR MOTION 
FOR COUNCIL 
CONSIDERATION 
 
 
 
Administration will continue to report progress through regular Council 
updates, departmental reporting, and project-specific briefing notes 
requiring policy direction, budget approval, or strategic decisions. 
 
 

