WHEREAS Council recognizes that access to sustainable, high-quality health care services is essential to 
the health and well-being of residents throughout the Central Algoma health care catchment area; and 
WHEREAS Council attended a public presentation entitled ""Central Algoma Health Care- A Vision for 
the Future,"" where local physicians outlined the challenges impacting the long - term sustainability of 
health care services, including aging infrastructure, increasing patient needs, changing demographics, 
and physician recruitment and retention challenges associated with the current health care delivery 
model; and 
WHEREAS Council recognizes the important role of hospitals, physician practices, nurse practitioner-led 
clinics, and other community health care partners for proactively identifying these challenges and 
bringing forward a collaborative vision to strengthen health care services for current and future 
generations; 
NOW THEREFORE BE IT RESOLVED THAT the Council of the Corporation of the Township of Johnson 
supports the principles and objectives of the Central Algoma Health Care - A Vision for the Future 
initiative and supports and encourages the establishment of a collaborative working group comprised of 
municipalities, physicians, health care organizations, and community representatives to advance 
planning for a sustainable health care model for the Central Algoma health care catchment area: and 
BE IT FURTHER RESOLVED THAT Council supports the evaluation of opportunities to enhance the long- 
term sustainability of health care services, including physician recruitment and retention strategies, 
continued support for local primary health care services, and the consideration of a new health care 
facility to meet the future needs of the communities served; and 
BE IT FURTHER RESOLVED THAT the Council of the Corporation of the Township of Johnson respectfully 
encourage municipalities, health care organizations, and community partners within the Central Algoma 
health care catchment area to support this initiative and participate in the collaborative planning 
process; and 
BE IT FURTHER RESOLVED THAT a copy of this resolution be forwarded to municipalities within the 
Central Algoma health care catchment area, the Boards of the Thessalon Hospital and St. Joseph Island 
Hospital, the local physicians and health care partners, the North Shore Health Network, the Honorable 
Sylvia Jones, Deputy Premier and Minister of Health, and Bill Rosenberg MPP for Algoma-Manitoulin, for 
their information and consideration. (cd) 
Res: 2026-141 E. McKinnon, K. Stobie 
BE IT RESOLVED THAT COUNCIL support the Physicians of Central Algoma and the North Shore 
Health Network in the continuous work to strengthen the healthcare services and better meet 
the needs of residents currently served by Bruce Mines Health Clinic and Thessalon and 
Richards Landing-Matthews sites. (cd) 

