Seconded by George Way 
 
RESOLVED THAT the Council of the Township of South-West Oxford receive report CL 
38-2026: Memorial Tree Planting - Councillor Valerie Durston as information; 
  
AND FURTHER THAT Council defer the decision on a memorial tree planting, and 
direct staff to bring the recommendation back to Council after a final decision is made 
for the advancement of the new municipal office, library and child care building.  
DISPOSITION: Motion Carried 
 
WD 9-2026: Brownsville Community Centre / Fire Hall – Generator Installation 
  
Public Works Superintendent Adam Prouse presented the report to Council requesting 
approval for the purchase and installation of a back up generator at the Brownsville 
Community Center/Fire Hall.  
  
Resolution No.6 
Moved by Paul Buchner 
Seconded by Peter Ypma 
 
RESOLVED THAT the Council of the Township of South-West Oxford receive Report 
WD 9-2026 as information;  

Council Minutes - October 06, 2026 
  
AND FURTHER THAT Council authorize staff to proceed with the purchase and 
installation of a new standby generator at the Brownsville Community Centre / Fire Hall 
in accordance with Section 16.0 of the Township's Purchasing Policy and the project be 
awarded to Smith Services for the quoted amount of $105,180.48 plus applicable taxes 
as a sole-source procurement. 
DISPOSITION: Motion Carried 
 
 
DISCUSSION ITEMS 
Township of Blandford-Blenheim - Skills Development Fund Grant 
 
Council requested comments from Fire Chief Shane Caskanette. Chief Caskanette 
recommended that Council support the resolution from the Township of Blandford-
Blenheim.  
  
Resolution No.7 
Moved by Craig Gillis 
Seconded by Peter Ypma 
 
RESOLVED THAT Council for the Township of South-West Oxford support the 
resolution from the Township of Blandford-Blenheim associated with Skills Development 
Fund. 
DISPOSITION: Motion Carried 
 
Councillor Pickard - Sweaburg Lions Community Park - Fence Cost Sharing  
  
Resolution No.8 
Moved by Jim Pickard 
Seconded by George Way 
 
RESOLVED THAT Council for the Township of South-West Oxford approve an 
additional $753.87 for the cost-sharing request for fence on the north side of Sweaburg 
Lions Park and that the funding be taken from the recreation reserve. 
DISPOSITION: Motion Carried 
 
Council moved the following item down on the agenda from 'Staff Reports': 
DD-08-2026: Petition for Drainage Works (Oxford Road 10) 
 
CBO/Drainage Superintendent Daniel Leduc presented the report to Council bringing 
forward a Petition for Drainage Works, submitted in accordance with Section 4 of the 
Drainage Act by Oxford County Road Authority for drainage along County Road 10 in 
the north end of Brownsville.  
  
Resolution No.9 
Moved by Jim Pickard 

Council Minutes - October 06, 2026 
Seconded by George Way 
 
RESOLVED THAT the Council of the Township of South-West Oxford accept the 
Petition for Drainage Works received from Oxford County Road Authority  
  
AND FURTHER THAT the firm of Spriet Associates Ltd., be appointed to complete a 
new report in accordance with Section 4 of the Drainage Act, RSO 1990, Chapter D17. 
DISPOSITION: Motion Carried 
 
Councillor Buchner - Speeding in Brownsville 
  
Councillor Buchner advised he has received phone calls from concerned residents 
regarding the speeding in Brownsville. Residents have requested the installation of 
automated speed signs at all four entrances to Brownsville, and the same request has 
been received from the residents of Culloden as well. Some residents have suggested 
the installation of high-visible delineators as well.  
  
Mayor Mayberry advised Oxford County is planning to undertake a speed study in 2027 
and look at installing automated speed signs on every county road that leads to an 
urban settlement area. 
  
Councillor Gillis - Drainage Report 
 
Councillor Gillis requested staff bring a report back to Council regarding the drainage 
fee now being collected in all villages to provide background information on the purpose 
of the charge and what the collection of the funds is utilized for. 
  
 
