Capital Delivery Observations 
The most significant delivered project in the review period is the Gagnon Road Bridge replacement. This directly 
addresses the highest-priority bridge item identified in the 2025 AMP. The Municipal Building project has advanced from 
long-term identified need to an external-funding application, but construction has not yet been authorized or completed 
through the AMP process. 
The remaining AMP priorities are not all intended to be delivered in a single year. The AMP assigns different timing 
horizons to projects and recommends that the Township prioritize work based on risk, condition and available funding. 
3. LEVELS OF SERVICE (LOS) AND RISK REVIEW 
 

