Risk Prioritization 
The AMP recommends a risk-based approach rather than replacing assets solely according to age. The model considers 
safety hazards, service-interruption risk and legal/compliance issues, and prioritizes high-risk or high-use assets while 
extending the useful life of lower-risk assets through targeted maintenance. The Gagnon Road Bridge replacement is 
consistent with that approach because the bridge was identified as a poor-condition asset requiring immediate action. 
