COMMUNITY HALL 
 
Present: 
 
 
Council: M. Mageran 
E. Caputo 
M. Christenson 
T. Trutenko 
 
 
 
Staff:  Megha Trivedi, Prateek Joshi 
 
 
Media: Maguerite LaHaye  
Public: Rose Zgraja 
 
Absent/Regret:  
 
 
Council: J. Weir 
 
1. Call to Order at 6:00 PM 
 
2. Approve Agenda 
Resolution 2026-157  
 
Moved by: Councillor E. Caputo 
 
 
Seconded by: Councillor M. Christenson 
 
BE IT RESOLVED THAT COUNCIL hereby accepts the agenda for Tuesday August 04th, 2026, and 
any addendums, as presented. (Carried)  
 
3. Disclosure of Pecuniary Interest- None 
 
4. Questions and Information Arising out of Minutes not Otherwise on Agenda- None 
 
5. Staff Reports 
a) Antique Farm Shed – Contents Report  
Resolution 2026-158  
Moved by: Councillor M. Christenson 
 
Seconded by: Councillor E. Caputo 
 
BE IT RESOLVED THAT Council hereby receives the report prepared by Rita Wagner regarding 
the ownership of the equipment and contents located within the Antique Farm Equipment 
Shed. (Carried and Recorded Vote) 
 
b) Clerk’s Report – Aug 2026 
Resolution 2026-159 
Moved by: Councillor E. Caputo  
 
 
Seconded by: Councillor T. Trutenko 
 

BE IT RESOLVED THAT Council hereby receives the Clerk-Treasurer's Report respecting the 
Antique Farm Equipment Shed. (Carried and Recorded Vote) 
 
6. 
By-Laws 
a) Bylaw 2026 – 33 Central Algoma Compliance Audit Joint Committee 
Resolution 2026-160 
Moved by: Councillor E. Caputo 
 
 
Seconded by: Councillor M. Christenson 
 
BE IT RESOLVED THAT By-Law 2026-33, being a by-law to appoint the Central Algoma 
Compliance Audit Joint Committee as the Compliance Audit Committee for the Township of 
Prince, be given a FIRST, SECOND and THIRD READING and FINALLY PASSED this 4th day of 
August 2026. (Carried) 
 
7. Correspondence 
Norquay Engineering – Structural Assessment Report – Antique Farm Equipment Shed 
Resolution 2026-161 
Moved by: Councillor T. Trutenko 
 
 
Seconded by: Councillor E. Caputo 
 
BE IT RESOLVED THAT Council hereby receives the Structural Assessment Report prepared by 
Norquay Engineering respecting the Antique Farm Equipment Shed. (Carried and Recorded 
Vote) 
 
8. New Business 
a) Antique Farm Equipment Shed – Disposition of Equipment and Contents 
Resolution 2026-162 
Moved by: Councillor M. Christenson 
 
Seconded by: Councillor E. Caputo 
 
BE IT RESOLVED THAT Council hereby directs staff to retain all equipment and contents 
currently located within the Antique Farm Equipment Shed, relocate the larger equipment to 
the area behind the Pavilion, and store the remaining smaller equipment and contents in a 
secure Sea Can pending future direction from the council. (Carried and Recorded Vote) 
 
