Notice to Residents
Please place your household waste and recycling at the
roadside on your scheduled collection day. Placing materials
at the roadside only on collection day helps deter birds and
animals.
Please note: Property owners are responsible for collecting
any waste or recycling that may be scattered along the
roadside by birds or animals.
Collection may take place anytime between 7:00 a.m. and
3:00 p.m. on your scheduled collection day. Please ensure
your waste and recycling are at the roadside before 7:00 a.m.
Garbage
Household waste must be placed in securely tied garbage
bags.
Approved removable containers may be used, provided
all household waste is securely contained in garbage bags.
Freezers and permanent containers are not permitted for
waste collection.Garbage must be placed at the side of the
nearest Township-maintained road or public highway for
collection.
Recycling
Fibre and GMP products must be placed in the recycling
bins provided.
Recycling must be placed at the side of the nearest
Township-maintained road or public highway for
collection.
Private Bins & Containers
Residents who use private bins or boxes to store household
waste or recycling must remove the materials from these
containers on the day of collection and place them at the
roadside as outlined above.
Private bins and boxes must remain on private property and
outside the obvious road allowance when they are not being
used for collection.
Waste & Recycling Collection Guidelines
WASTE DISPOSAL AND FEES
A Waste Disposal Site Pass must be shown to the attendant to dispose of waste at both
landfill sites. If you are new to the township and require a pass please contact the office.
Replacement passes can be purchased for $10.00 at the township office.  
Please note  your waste pass does not expire.
Only waste generated from within the geographic boundaries of the Township of South
Algonquin shall be deposited in the landfill site. Waste Disposal Site Pass or Demolition
Permit must be provided. Only domestic, construction and demolition waste, scrap
metal/appliances and tires are accepted for disposal at the landfill sites. Hazardous 
waste, septic waste and liquid industrial waste are not accepted.
 
 
