Message from the Mayor
As we welcome the autumn season, I would
like to wish everyone a very happy and
enjoyable fall. This is such a beautiful time
of year in South Algonquin, with vibrant
colours, sunny days, and many activities
taking place throughout our communities.
The Township continues to be busy with
several important initiatives. Work on the
new Comprehensive Zoning By-law is well
underway, and staff are also working on the
Township’s Boat Launch and Trails Master
Plan, which will help guide future planning
and improvements to these important
community assets.
There are also many community events and
activities to look forward to in the coming
months. I encourage everyone to get
involved, support our local organizations
and volunteers, and enjoy all that South
Algonquin has to offer this fall.  
I would also like to take a moment to
remember former Councillors Dave Harper,
Sidney James, and Robert Ogilvie, who are
no longer with us, as well as Jackie Wilson,
a dedicated Township employee who
brought joy and laughter to everyone
around her. Jackie will also be fondly
remembered for her pleasant smile and the
warm welcome she provided to everyone
who came to the front counter.
Each of them was a valued member of our
community, and their loss is felt by many.
We extend our sincere condolences to their
families, friends, and all those who knew
them. Their contributions to the Township
and their connections to our community will
be fondly remembered. 
As always, I welcome the opportunity to
hear from residents. If you would like to
meet with me or discuss a Township matter,
please contact the Township Office Ext.205
or call 613-332-8357.  
I hope everyone has a safe and enjoyable
autumn season! 
Mayor LaValley
