3(a) The Minutes of September 23, 2026 were accepted as circulated. 
    
4. BUSINESS ARISING: 
There was no business arising. 
 
5. PROCLAMATION: 
a. Mi’kmaq History Month 
 
5(a) Warden Smith read the Mi’kmaq History Month Proclamation, formally declaring October 2026 
Mi’kmaq History Month in the Municipality of the District of Shelburne. The document was included in 
the meeting package. 
 
6. PUBLIC HEARING: 
a. Land Use Bylaw Amendment, Rezoning PID 82573577 – Crystal Fuller, Brighter Community 
Planning & Consulting 
b. Public Comments 
 
MOTION: ENTER PUBLIC HEARING  
Being duly moved and seconded, be it resolved that the Council of the Municipality of the District 
of Shelburne enter into Public Hearing at 6:02pm. 
 
6(a) Warden Smith welcomed everyone to the Public Hearing regarding the amendment to the 
Municipality of Shelburne’s Land Use By-Law and outlined the intent and process for the Hearing.  
Chrystal Fuller, Municipal Planner with Brighter Community Planning and Consulting, presented 
Council and members of the public with a brief overview of the amendment to the Municipality of 
Shelburne’s Land Use By-Law. The presentation summarized the request of rezoning PID 82573577, 
the description of the property, and the planning analysis. 
 
Warden Smith thanked Ms. Fuller for presenting. 
 
6(b) Residents had the opportunity to submit written feedback regarding the Municipality of 
Shelburne’s Land Use Bylaw Amendment, Rezoning PID 82573577, and it was noted that no written 
submissions were received. Residents also had the opportunity to speak at the Hearing in person or 
virtually, and there were no requests received.  
 
 
MOTION: EXIT PUBLIC HEARING  
 
Being duly moved and seconded, be it resolved that the Council of the Municipality of the 
District of Shelburne exit Public Hearing at 6:12pm.  
- 
MOTION CARRIED 
 
 
 
 
Page 5

Council Meeting 
October 14, 2026 
7. ECONOMIC & COMMUNITY DEVELOPMENT: 
a. Land Use Bylaw Amendment, Rezoning PID 82573577, Second Reading – Chrystal Fuller, 
Brighter Community Planning & Consulting  
 
7(a) Warden Penny Smith noted the Land Use Bylaw Amendment, Rezoning PID 82573577, Second 
Reading staff report details were included in item 6(a). 
 
 
MOTION: REZONING PID 82573577, SECOND READING 
 
Be it resolved that the Council of the Municipality of the District of Shelburne give second and 
final reading to amend the Land Use By-law Zoning Map to rezone PID 82573577, located on 
Sandy Point Road, Sandy Point, from the Residential (RES) Zone to the General Industrial (GI) 
Zone. 
- 
MOTION CARRIED 
 
8. OPERATIONS: 
a. Monthly Building Report – September 2026 
b. Construction Projects and Permits – Andrew Goreham, Manager of Inspection Services 
 
8(a) Warden Smith reviewed the Monthly Building Report for August 2026. 
 
8(b) Andrew Goreham, Manager of Inspection Services presented the Construction Projects and 
Permits staff report. 
Mr. Goreham advised Council that building permits decreased overall in 2025 – 2026 compared to 
previous years, with new dwelling construction remaining comparatively strong with 34 new dwelling 
permits issued in 2025 – 2026. Mr. Goreham also stated the trends for 2026-2027 show a decrease in 
permit activity as of the end of September.   
