PROCLAMATION 
Mi’kmaq History Month 
October 2026 
WHEREAS Mi’kmaq History Month was established in 1993 by the Province of Nova Scotia 
in partnership with the Mi’kmaq Grand Council, to recognize and celebrate Mi’kmaq 
culture and heritage; and 
WHEREAS October is recognized as Mi’kmaq History Month, providing an opportunity to 
recognize, celebrate, and learn about the history, culture, traditions, and contributions of 
the Mi’kmaq people; and
WHEREAS the Municipality of the District of Shelburne is located on the ancestral and 
unceded territory of the Mi’kmaq People, and acknowledges the importance of honouring 
this enduring connection; and 
WHEREAS recognizing Mi’kmaq history and culture contributes to building stronger 
relationships, promoting reconciliation, and fostering greater understanding and respect 
among all people; and
WHEREAS the Municipality of Shelburne recognizes the importance of learning from and 
celebrating the rich history, culture, and ongoing contributions of the Mi’kmaq people; 
THEREFORE be it resolved that I, Penny Smith, Warden for the Municipality of the District of 
Shelburne, do hereby proclaim October 2026 as Mi’kmaq History Month in the Municipality 
of the District of Shelburne. 
We encourage all residents to take part in opportunities to learn, reflect, celebrate, and 
recognize the significant contributions of the Mi’kmaq people to our community and 
region. 
