5.1 Amendments to Decisions - VRH-02 and VRH-03

 
TO:    
Mayor and Council, Township of Val Rita-Harty  
FROM:   
Josh Young, CPT Planner (E4m Consultant)    
DATE:   
October 29th, 2026 
RE:    
Amendment to Conditions of Consent Approval: 
 Files VRH-002 and VRH-003 
   
Recommendation 
Resolution: 
THAT the Committee of Adjustment recommend that Council amend the conditions of 
approval for Consent Applications VRH-002 and VRH-003 to reflect the current 
ownership and parcel configuration, as outlined in the Planning Report. 
 
Background 
Council approved Consent Applications VRH-002 and VRH-003 subject to conditions 
intended to address title, parcel configuration and the implementation of the proposed 
severances. 
 
The applicants subsequently requested municipal sign-off to facilitate the issuance of 
the Certificates of Consent. A review of the files identified outstanding conditions that 
had not been satisfied. As the Clerk cannot waive or amend conditions imposed by 
Council, the Certificates of Consent could not be issued. 
 
Following discussions/meetings that took place with the Applicants it was identified that 
there had been changes to the ownership and parcel configuration following Council's 
decision. These changes significantly affect certain conditions, some of which can no 
longer be satisfied and require consideration of an amendment to the original approvals 
to provide the required Certificates of Consent. 
 
The Applicants have therefore requested that the conditions be amended to reflect the 
current circumstances of the lands.   
 
Planning Analysis 
The original planning review was based on the ownership, parcel configuration and 
information available when Council considered the applications. 
 
Subsequent changes to the subject lands have affected the implementation of certain 
conditions. The requested amendments are intended to address these changes and 
establish conditions that can be satisfied while maintaining the intent of the original 
approvals. 
Planning Report | Page - 8
6.1 Committee of Adjustment Business

 
The proposed amendments do not change the overall land division contemplated by the 
applications or the planning considerations that supported the original decisions. They 
are intended to address the outstanding matters arising from the current ownership and 
parcel configuration so the consent process can proceed. 
 
Planning Opinion 
In my professional opinion, the requested amendments are appropriate, provided the 
revised conditions continue to satisfy the applicable planning requirements and maintain 
the intent of Council's original decisions. 
 
The original recommendations were based on the circumstances and information 
available at the time. The subsequent changes to the subject lands have affected the 
Applicants' ability to fulfil certain conditions as originally imposed. An amendment to the 
conditions is therefore being brought forward for consideration through the appropriate 
planning process. 
 
