10.1 Electronic Devices and Cellular Telephones
To protect the confidentiality of matters considered during a Closed Meeting, no cellular 
telephones, smart phones, tablets, smart watches, recording devices, personal 
computers, or other personal electronic communication devices shall be permitted 
within the Closed Meeting room or Council Chambers during a Closed Meeting unless 
specifically authorized for municipal business.
Prior to the commencement of a Closed Meeting:
1. All Members of Council, staff, consultants, guests, and any other persons 
authorized to attend the Closed Meeting shall surrender all personal electronic 
devices to the Clerk for secure safekeeping.
2. Where the Clerk is attending the Closed Meeting virtually, devices shall be 
surrendered to a designated staff member who is participating in the open 
meeting in person or the Mayor in the absence of a staff person.
3. The Clerk, Mayor, or designated staff member receiving the devices shall 
maintain custody of the devices until the Closed Meeting has concluded.
4. Municipal-issued devices required for the conduct of business may be permitted 
with the approval of the Clerk, provided that all recording, photography, video, 
audio capture, communication, wireless transmission, and internet connectivity 
functions are disabled before the commencement of the Closed Meeting.
5. No person attending a Closed Meeting shall record, photograph, transmit, 
livestream, copy, or otherwise capture any portion of the Closed Meeting 
proceedings.
Failure to comply with this section may result in the attendee being required to leave the 
Closed Meeting and may be reported to Council for further action under the 
Municipality's applicable by-laws, policies, procedures, or Code of Conduct.
