Dear Mayor and Council: 
As your new term of Council begins, please accept our congratulations and best wishes for the next four years. 
Under the District Social Services Administration Boards Act, the current DSSAB Board term ends on December 
31, 2026. To ensure uninterrupted representation and service to the District, Council is asked to appoint two (2) 
members of Council to represent Area 5 on the DSSAB Board for the new term of January 1, 2027, to December 
31, 2030. These two (2) members must be jointly appointed from all 6 councils that make up the municipalities 
in your Area in order for there to be representation on the DSSAB Board. 
 
Area Five consists of the Village of South River, Village of Sundridge, Township of Joly, Township of Machar, 
Township of Strong and Township of Magnetawan. This area is currently represented by Teri Brandt (South River) 
and Sharon Smith (Sundridge). 
We would appreciate receiving a resolution from your Council confirming appointments as early as possible 
following the municipal election. Early appointments will allow DSSAB staff to formally establish new Board 
members and distribute orientation and training materials in advance of the first Board meeting. 
 
The first Board meeting of the new term is scheduled for Thursday, January 14, 2027, at 6:30 p.m., by virtual 
meeting. DSSAB Board meetings are normally held virtually on the second Thursday of each month at 6:30 p.m. 
Should you have any questions, please do not hesitate to contact me at 705-746-7777 Ext. 5264 or 
jblower@psdssab.org. 
 
Sincerely, 
 
