Board Honoraria and Expenses - Revision October 8, 2026 
BOARD HONORARIA AND EXPENSES 
1. PURPOSE 
To establish a transparent, fiscally responsible, and service-based framework for compensating members of the 
District of Parry Sound Social Services Administration Board (DSSAB). 
2. POLICY STATEMENT 
Board service is a public responsibility carried out on behalf of the municipalities in the District of Parry Sound. 
Board members shall be compensated only for attendance at eligible meetings and Board-approved conferences 
or training events, as set out in this policy. 
Board members shall be reimbursed for eligible travel and expenses incurred while attending eligible meetings or 
approved conferences or training events, subject to this policy. 
3. SCOPE 
This policy applies to: 
• 
All DSSAB Board members; 
• 
The Chair and Vice-Chair; and 
• 
Board-appointed committee members, where applicable. 
4. DEFINITIONS 
Eligible meeting. A Board, special Board, Board committee, or other meeting that is formally scheduled or duly 
called, has quorum where quorum is required, and is approved by the Board or required by statute, regulation, or 
by-law. 
Quorum not established. Where quorum is not established after the 30-minute waiting period set out in the 
Board’s procedural rules, each Board member in attendance shall be paid $50. No other meeting remuneration is 
payable for that meeting. 
Board-approved conference or training event. A conference, training event, or meeting outside regular or 
special Board meetings. 
Community event. A public, ceremonial, promotional, fundraising, stakeholder, or community-attendance activity 
where a board member is invited, but not required, to attend.  

Board Honoraria and Expenses - Revision October 8, 2026 
5. REMUNERATION FRAMEWORK 
5.1 Honoraria 
Honoraria for eligible meetings attended shall be paid as follows: 
Role / Meeting Type 
Compensation 
Chair 
 $700.00 per month, plus $230.00 per eligible regular 
or special Board meeting attended. 
Vice-Chair 
$185.00 per eligible regular or special Board meeting 
attended. 
Board member 
$150.00 per eligible meeting attended. 
Committee meeting immediately before or after a 
duly called Board or Board committee meeting 
75% of the applicable regular Board member meeting 
rate. 
 
The Chair and Vice-Chair rates apply only to eligible regular or special Board meetings. Where the Chair or Vice-
Chair attends another eligible meeting, the applicable Board member rate applies. 
5.2 Board-Approved Conferences and Training Events 
Attendance at Board-approved conferences or training events by any member, Chair, or Vice-Chair, is recognized 
at the applicable regular Board member meeting rate. Attendance and approval shall be documented. 
5.3 Non-Compensable Activities 
Compensation shall not be paid for: 
• 
Cancelled meetings, including adjourned meetings that do not proceed, except for the $50 payment described 
under “Quorum not established” above; 
• 
Informal briefings or workshops; 
• 
Reading or preparation time; or 
• 
Community events where participation is not a Board requirement. 
6. TRAVEL AND EXPENSE REIMBURSEMENT 
6.1 Travel 
Board members may be reimbursed for reasonable and necessary expenses incurred while attending eligible 
meetings or Board-approved conferences or training events, subject to Board authorization and supporting 
documentation. 
• 
