Subject: Consents B-2026-0033-34-H and Zoning By-law Amendment R-2026-0019-H (Rettie) 
From: Bradie Debes, RPP, Planner, Planning Department  
Agenda Date: November 2, 2026 
Report No: PL-2026-112 
Executive Summary: 
 
The purpose of the consent applications is to create two new rural residential lots with frontage 
on Marlyn Drive. 
The purpose of the associated Zoning By-law Amendment is to rezone the proposed severed 
lots to Rural Residential Exception Zones for compliance with minimum lot frontage and area 
requirements and to implement minimum setbacks from natural features.  
It is recommended that any public comments be considered, and the applications approved 
accordingly.   
 
 

