The purpose and effect of the proposed consent applications is to create two new rural 
residential lots. The proposed Severed Lot 1 would have an area of approximately 1.2 hectares 
and 91 metres of frontage on Marlyn Drive. The proposed Severed Lot 2 would have an area 
of approximately 2.3 hectares and 185.3 metres of frontage on Marlyn Drive. The proposed 
Retained Lot would have a resulting lot area of approximately 7.9 hectares and would 
maintain 160 metres of shoreline lot frontage on the Seguin River. The proposed Retained Lot 
would have a resulting 387.05 metres of road frontage on Turtle Lake Road and 40 metres of 
road frontage on Marlyn Drive. 
The purpose and effect of the associated Zoning By-law Amendment is to rezone the 
proposed Severed Lots 1 and 2 from the Rural Exception Thirty One (RU-31) Zone to Rural 
Residential Exception Zones for compliance with minimum lot frontage and area requirements 

