Public Participation & Access 
 
Notice of the application was circulated and posted in accordance with the Planning Act. 
Notice was also posted on the Township’s website. 
 
Comments of no concern have been received from Hydro One.  
 
Land Use Planning Policy 
 
Planning Act 
 
The applications have been reviewed against Section 2 of the Planning Act and are in 
accordance with the applicable provincial interests.  
 
The applications have been evaluated against the criteria set out under Section 51(24) of 
the Planning Act. The proposal conforms to the Official Plan, is suited to the topography of 
the subject lands, and can be adequately serviced without impacting the public interest. 
The application has full regard for all matters listed under Section 51(24) of the Act and 
constitutes good land-use planning. 
 
Provincial Planning Statement, 2024 (PPS) and Growth Plan for Northern Ontario (GPNO) 
 
The Provincial Planning Statement is a province-wide document requiring consistency of all 
decisions with its policies. 
 
The subject lands are classified as Rural Lands in the PPS. Section 2.6.1 recognizes residential 
development as a permitted use on Rural Lands if site conditions are suitable for appropriate 
sewage and water services. A condition of approval requires the applicant to obtain 
confirmation from the approval authority of a suitable septic system envelope for any future 
development on the proposed severed lots. 
 
Section 4 of the PPS and Section 6 of the GPNO address matters relating to the wise use and 
management of resources. It is noted under Section 4.1 of the PPS that natural features and 
areas shall be protected for the long term.  
 

Seguin Township 
Staff Report to Council 
 
 
 
 
Staff Report No. PL-2026-112 
Page 6 of 10 
A wetland exists close to the southern boundary of the property and is identified as 
Environmental Protection within the Official Plan and Zoning By-law.  
 
The proposed zoning by-law amendment will rezone the proposed Severed Lot 2 to ensure 
that a development setback of 50 metres from the environmental protection area exists for 
future buildings and structures. 
 
The applications are consistent with the policies of the PPS and with the guiding policies of 
the GPNO. 
 
Township of Seguin Official Plan 
 
The subject lands are located within the Rural and Resource Area and Environmental 
Protection designation in the Official Plan. Permitted uses within the Rural and Resource Area 
include low-density residential uses, small-scale industrial and commercial uses, agriculture, 
forestry and home occupations and home industries. The proposed applications seek to 
sever two new rural residential lots from the Rural and Resource Area. It is the objective of the 
Rural and Resource Area designation to permit limited new development that is compatible 
with the rural environment. It is also an objective to buffer adjacent lands and uses from the 
potential negative impact of the uses permitted with the Rural and Resource Area 
designation.   
There are several sections of the Official Plan that must be considered for new lot creation. 
Section B.12.2.1 of the Official Plan lists requirements for new lot creation in all land use 
designations, such as frontage and area requirements, conformity to applicable Official Plan 
policies and the Planning Act, and servicing requirements. The proposal conforms to this 
policy set. 
In addition to the general Official Plan policies, Section B.12.2.5 of the Official Plan contains 
policies that apply to severances within the Rural and Resource Area designation. The 
creation of a new Rural Residential lot shall have a minimum lot size of 1.2 hectares and a 
minimum lot frontage of 90 metres. Lots of this size are acceptable in areas of established 
rural residential development. It shall be noted that rural residential development exists to  
the north and east of the property. The applicants propose to rezone the severed lots from 
the Rural Exception Thirty-One (RU-31) Zone to the Rural Residential Exception Eighty-Six and 
Eighty-Seven (RR-86 and RR-87) zones for compliance with lot frontage and area 
requirements for the RR zone.  

Seguin Township 
Staff Report to Council 
 
 
 
 
Staff Report No. PL-2026-112 
Page 7 of 10 
Per the Official Plan, Star Lake is identified as a Lake Trout Lake at Capacity. The proposed 
severed lots will be located within 300 metres of the Seguin River, which flows into Star Lake.  
 
Section B.3 indicates that new development is not permitted within 300 metres of lakes or 
permanently inflowing streams to these waterbodies with this classification as a 
precautionary approach to protect water quality.  In this case, the associated Zoning By-law 
Amendment would place an exception on the severed lots to ensure that future septic 
system components are located 300 metres from the shoreline of the Seguin River. This will 
ensure that water quality of downstream Star Lake and the Seguin River is protected. 
 
